  {"a":"warwick","b":"aatrox","win":["Warwick","Warwick","Aatrox","Aatrox","Aatrox","Aatrox","Aatrox"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Jaws of the Beast heals and Blood Hunt speeds you at him, but bait The Darkin Blade — 14s at rank 1 — then step in, and never trade into his third swing edge."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Infinite Duress suppresses 1.5s and Umbral Dash cannot break it, so it beats his reposition; all-in when Blood Hunt lights him up below 50%, and never into a fresh World Ender."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Rushing an early bruiser item keeps you tankier than Aatrox's first spike; his Deathdance/Eclipse timing is when he starts winning extended fights."},{"when":"Late","text":"Once Aatrox has 2+ items his three-Q rotation plus healing on the sweet spots out-DPSes and out-sustains you in drawn-out fights, so pick him off before he ults."}],"wants":{"you":["Bait out Aatrox's Q edges then trade in the dead zones","Use W Blood Hunt to chase when he's below 50% and E to eat his Q knockup","Ult during his Q windup to cancel the cast and suppress him"],"foe":["Land the sweet spot of all three Qs to knock you up and heal","Save E dash to dodge your R and reposition","Stall trades until his ult and items let him out-sustain you"]},"early":"You bully the early lane: Q's on-cast heal plus W attack speed win the auto-trades while Aatrox has only one Q and no reliable knockup rhythm yet, so poke him off the wave and don't let him free-stack.","mid":"Levels 3-6 are yours except the level-4/5 window where his Q combo comes online — trade in the gaps between his Q edges, and at 6 your R suppress beats his mobility, letting you all-in when Blood Hunt lights him up.","late":"Aatrox flips the matchup with items: his healing on the Q sweet spots and Deathdance revive out-sustain your DPS in long fights, so end the game early or force short bursts with R rather than brawling him even.","whys":["Level 1 is yours because your Q heal and passive sustain beat Aatrox's single-Q trade before he has combo rhythm.","Level 2 stays yours as W attack speed swings extended autos in your favour while his knockup timing is unreliable.","Level 3 goes to Aatrox: the full Darkin Blade chain plus Umbral Dash healing outlasts your Q bite.","Levels 4-5 are his: The Darkin Blade drops toward 8s and Infernal Chains grounds your Q dash if you sit in the zone.","Level 6 tilts Aatrox: World Ender's heal amp outlasts a lone 1.5s Infinite Duress if you burn R early.","At first item Aatrox pulls ahead: his lifesteal spike plus Umbral Dash healing beats your bruiser item.","With 2+ items Aatrox wins — three-Q healing plus Deathdance out-sustains and out-DPSes you in long fights."]},
  {"a":"warwick","b":"akali","win":["Skill","Akali","Akali","Skill","Skill","Akali","Akali"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Before Akali's E is maxed her all-in is weak; your Q heal and W attack speed win short trades, so punish every time she walks up to last-hit and force her to spend energy early."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Infinite Duress collides rather than targets, so Twilight Shroud's untargetability does not stop it — leap the instant she commits, and never spend it chasing her into the smoke."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Akali's first item (Hextech/Nashor's) is her power spike; her E-Q-R burst starts one-shotting squishies and she can dodge your gap-close with her second R dash."},{"when":"Late","text":"With items Akali kites your engage with shroud invisibility and two R dashes, resetting fights faster than you can lock her; you need flash or ally CC to pin her."}],"wants":{"you":["Trade early while her E is low-rank and energy is scarce","Ult on reaction to her commit so shroud can't save her","Leap R through the shroud — it collides, it does not target"],"foe":["Farm safely with Five Point Strike and shroud until level 6","Wait for first item then E-Q burst you before you can close","Use both R dashes and shroud to disengage your all-in"]},"early":"You own the opening levels: Akali is energy-starved and her E dash is weak at rank 1, so your Q heal and W attack speed win every short trade — walk her down when she steps up to CS.","mid":"Level 3 and level 6 are yours because your kit out-trades her pre-item and R suppress ignores her mobility, but the level-2 and level-4/5 windows are skill-dependent as she starts weaving shroud and E resets into her poke.","late":"Once Akali has an item she flips it: her burst combo deletes you before you brawl and shroud plus double-R dash lets her escape your Duress, so play for ganks and ally CC rather than a solo all-in.","whys":["Level 1 is a coin flip: Five Point Strike pokes free, but Q sustain beats her rank-1 E trade.","Level 2 is skill-based as she starts using shroud and passive poke to even the exchange.","Level 3 goes to Akali once Twilight Shroud is up — she farms untargetable and your Q needs a target.","Levels 4-5 read even — she gains E-reset pressure while you keep sustain, so outcomes depend on execution.","Level 6 is even: Duress collides and suppresses, but Perfect Execution answers it.","At first item Akali wins as her burst combo one-shots and out-ranges your engage.","With 2+ items she stays ahead — shroud invisibility and double-R dash reset fights faster than you can lock her."]},
  {"a":"warwick","b":"akshan","win":["Akshan","Skill","Warwick","Warwick","Akshan","Warwick","Warwick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Akshan's level-2 spike with W and E swing lets him poke and reposition, but once you hit 3 your Q heal closes the gap on his ranged autos; walk him down through minions to negate his range."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Infinite Duress suppresses him mid-swing and cancels the Heroic Swing reposition, but CC on you breaks it — Blood Hunt's move speed also makes the leap travel further."},{"when":"1st item","text":"You keep the edge post-item because Akshan is squishy and your bruiser sustain lets you survive his combo and lock him with R for the kill."},{"when":"Late","text":"Even late your R catches his low-HP frame; fight in tight terrain where he has no swing anchor, and Blood Hunt's bonus move speed lengthens the leap."}],"wants":{"you":["Walk Akshan down through the wave to shut off his auto poke","Save R to cancel his Heroic Swing mid-flight","Let Blood Hunt speed stretch your R leap onto him"],"foe":["Abuse level-2 W passive shield and E poke to zone you","Kite backward with autos and reposition off terrain with E","Roam with E swing to snowball other lanes since he can't beat your all-in"]},"early":"Akshan's Avengerang out-ranges you at 1, and his level-2 poke plus passive shield out-trades you — hold Primal Howl for his step-up: 2.5s of damage reduction, then a 1s fear, and walk him down once you hit 3.","mid":"The level-3 to level-5 window is skill-dependent as you close range through minions against his kiting, but at 6 respect Comeuppance: Infinite Duress cancels Heroic Swing, yet any CC on you breaks the suppression.","late":"You stay favoured into items because Akshan is fragile and your R catches his low-HP frame through his mobility; fight in tight terrain, and let Blood Hunt's move speed stretch the leap onto him.","whys":["Level 1 is Akshan's: Avengerang out-ranges you before Jaws of the Beast is online.","Level 2 favours Akshan — his W passive shield and E poke let him zone and out-range you.","Level 3 is skill-based as you work to close his range through the wave while he kites.","Levels 4-5 stay even, decided by whether you can pin him or he kites cleanly.","Level 6 goes to Akshan: Comeuppance punishes you low and CC breaks your R.","At first item you lead because your sustain survives his burst and R locks his squishy frame.","With 2+ items you stay ahead — R hard-catches his low-HP body through his mobility."]},
  {"a":"warwick","b":"ambessa","win":["Skill","Warwick","Warwick","Skill","Skill","Warwick","Warwick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Cunning Sweep only transforms into Sundering Slam after it strikes you, so step out after her first Q; Jaws of the Beast is back in 7s, and Repudiation pays off only if she blocks damage while bracing."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Public Execution blinks to the farthest champion in line and suppresses — 130s at rank 1. Fight that window: Infinite Duress collides, so she cannot just dash out."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Blade of the Ruined King is your spike: max-health damage plus Eternal Hunger healing once you drop under 50% outlasts her burst, and Repudiation's shield is a one-off."},{"when":"Late","text":"Late you catch her: Blood Hunt turns on under 50% and triples under 25%, and that bonus move speed makes your Infinite Duress leap travel further onto her."}],"wants":{"you":["Bait Cunning Sweep, then trade before it transforms","Only ult after she's blown her dashes so she can't escape","Brawl under 50% — that is when your passive heals"],"foe":["Chain Cunning Sweep into Sundering Slam to chunk your trades","Reset her dashes off your minions to stay untouchable","Land Public Execution once you're chunked low"]},"early":"Level 1 is a coin flip, then 2 and 3 are yours — Jaws of the Beast deals max-health damage and Primal Howl gives 2.5s of damage reduction before its 1s fear, so take the step-up trade.","mid":"Levels 3-5 are yours and 6 reads even: her combo chunks you, but Eternal Hunger only heals once you are under 50%, so a low brawl is correct here — and Public Execution's 130s is the window to force.","late":"You keep the edge on items — max-health Q damage and Eternal Hunger's tripled healing under 25% beat her burst, and Infinite Duress collides rather than targets, so Drakehound's Step cannot shake it.","whys":["Level 1 is yours because your Q sustain beats Ambessa before her empowered combo is online.","Level 2 is skill-based as she gains her second ability and can start trading back.","Level 3 is yours: Jaws of the Beast eats max health while Lacerate is 13s at rank 1.","Levels 4-5 read even — Cunning Sweep chunks you, but your Q is back in 7s.","Level 6 reads even: Public Execution is 130s, and Primal Howl blunts her combo.","At first item you lead: Blade of the Ruined King out-sustains her burst.","With 2+ items Ambessa dominates — mobility dodges your R and her burst deletes you."]},
  {"a":"warwick","b":"aurora","win":["Warwick","Aurora","Skill","Skill","Warwick","Aurora","Aurora"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Aurora's W spirit-dash lets her sidestep your gap-close and her Q double-hit pokes you down; her level-2 spike is strong, so wait until you've closed range through minions before committing."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Infinite Duress collides with the first champion in its path, so Across the Veil only saves her if she blinks before you leap — all-in at 6 once Blood Hunt switches on under 50% health."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Aurora's first mage item spikes her burst; her Q-E poke plus W repositioning kite your engage and chunk you before you close, so respect her damage after her item."},{"when":"Late","text":"With items Aurora zones you with her R exile field and W dashes, poking you out of fights before you reach her; you need flash or ally CC to pin her down."}],"wants":{"you":["Close range through minions to negate her poke","Ult before she can W-dash out of your engage","Use Blood Hunt to sprint at her once she's under 50%"],"foe":["Poke with Q double-hit and E to chunk you pre-engage","W-dash to dodge your R and reposition to safety","Use R exile zone to isolate and burst you late"]},"early":"Level 1 is yours with Q sustain, but Across the Veil at 22s and Twofold Hex hand her the level-2 window — hold Primal Howl for it: 2.5s of damage reduction, then a 1s fear on the way out.","mid":"Levels 3-5 are skill-dependent as you fight through her kiting to land an engage, and level 6 swings to you: R Infinite Duress locks her through the W dodge if timed right, so all-in when she's revealed low.","late":"After her first item Aurora flips it — her burst and W repositioning let her poke you out and dodge your R, so you fall behind unless you have flash or a jungler to pin her for the Duress.","whys":["Level 1 is yours since your Q sustain beats Aurora before her W and poke come online.","Level 2 favours Aurora — her W dash and Q double-hit let her dodge and poke you.","Level 3 is skill-based as you close range through minions against her kite.","Levels 4-5 stay even, decided by whether you can pin her or she dashes clear.","Level 6 is yours: R Infinite Duress suppresses through her W dodge when timed right.","At first item Aurora wins — her mage spike and W repositioning kite your engage.","With 2+ items she stays ahead, zoning you with R exile and dodging your R with W."]},
  {"a":"warwick","b":"camille","win":["Warwick","Skill","Warwick","Warwick","Warwick","Camille","Camille"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Before Camille's Q double-cast and E are online you out-sustain her; your Q heal and W attack speed win extended trades, so punish her when she walks up to CS and force her to E away."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Infinite Duress collides and suppresses 1.5s, so Hookshot only escapes it if she leaves first; all-in at 6 when Blood Hunt lights her up below 50% health."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Camille's first item (Sheen/Divine Sunderer) is her spike — her Q true-damage second cast and E stun start winning trades, and her R can isolate you for a full combo."},{"when":"Late","text":"With items Camille out-DPSes and out-mobilities you: her E gap-close, Q resets and R cage dictate the fight, so pick her before she reaches you or peel her R with terrain."}],"wants":{"you":["Trade early before her Q recharges and E come online","Ult to cancel her E hookshot escape and lock her","Chase with Blood Hunt once she drops under 50%"],"foe":["Wait for first item then Q-E stun to out-trade you","Use E hookshot to dodge your R and reposition","Isolate you with R cage for a full unanswered combo"]},"early":"You win the opening lane: Precision Protocol at rank 1 cannot out-trade Jaws of the Beast, and Primal Howl's 2.5s of damage reduction eats her second cast — walk her down and spend her Hookshot.","mid":"Levels 3 through 6 are all yours — Jaws of the Beast beats her pre-item, and at 6 Infinite Duress collides and suppresses through the Hookshot escape, so all-in whenever Blood Hunt triggers.","late":"Camille flips it on items: her Q true damage, E stun and R isolation cage out-trade and out-mobility you in extended fights, so end early or force short bursts and use terrain to break her R cage.","whys":["Level 1 is yours since your Q sustain beats Camille's rank-1 kit in a trade.","Level 2 is skill-based as she gains a second ability and can start poking back.","Level 3 favours you because Q heal and W attack speed out-trade her pre-item.","Levels 4-5 stay yours as your sustain still beats her before her item spike.","Level 6 is yours: R Infinite Duress suppresses her out of the E hookshot escape.","At first item Camille wins — Q true damage and E stun out-trade you.","With 2+ items she stays ahead, using E, Q resets and R cage to out-DPS and isolate you."]},
  {"a":"warwick","b":"cassiopeia","win":["Warwick","Skill","Warwick","Cassiopeia","Cassiopeia","Cassiopeia","Cassiopeia"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Miasma grounds rather than roots: you can still walk, but Jaws of the Beast and Infinite Duress are both dead inside it — 24s at rank 1, so step in only once she has laid it and left it."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Petrifying Gaze stuns only enemies facing her — turn your back and it is a slow instead. Approach after Miasma is spent, because grounding, not the stun, is what kills your leap."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Cassiopeia's first mage item spikes her sustained poison DPS; her Q-E spam melts you before you close and W grounding cancels every dash, so you can't reach her cleanly."},{"when":"Late","text":"With items Cassiopeia kites you forever — W grounding negates your engage, R stuns your all-in and her poison out-DPSes your sustain, so you need flanks and ally CC to touch her."}],"wants":{"you":["Close range through minions before she lays W grounding","Engage from her flank so her R can't face-stun you","Ult right after she's used W so grounding is down"],"foe":["Ground your dash with W Miasma to shut off your engage","Stack Q-E poison to out-DPS your sustain from range","Face-stun your R with Petrifying Gaze to cancel the all-in"]},"early":"Level 1 is yours with Q sustain, and level 2 is skill-based, but from level 3 Cassiopeia's W grounding and Q poison start zoning you — close distance through the wave early before she can control the space.","mid":"Levels 4 through 6 belong to Cassiopeia: Miasma grounds both your dashes and is 24s at rank 1, and Petrifying Gaze stuns you only while you face her — engage after she has spent W.","late":"Cassiopeia runs the matchup late — grounding cancels your gap-close, R stuns your all-in and her poison out-DPSes your sustain, so play for flanks and jungle CC rather than a solo engage.","whys":["Level 1 is yours since your Q sustain beats Cassiopeia before her poison zone is online.","Level 2 is skill-based as she starts layering Q poison and you look to close range.","Level 3 favours you because you can still walk her down before W grounding is impactful.","Levels 4-5 flip to Cassiopeia — W Miasma grounds your dash and her poison out-DPSes you.","Level 6 is Cassiopeia's: R Petrifying Gaze face-stuns and cancels your Infinite Duress.","At first item she leads with sustained poison DPS that melts you before you close.","With 2+ items Cassiopeia dominates — grounding, R stun and poison keep you off her entirely."]},
  {"a":"warwick","b":"chogath","win":["Skill","Warwick","Warwick","Cho'Gath","Cho'Gath","Cho'Gath","Cho'Gath"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"With Jaws of the Beast healing you and Blood Hunt speeding you at a low target, you win extended trades before Vorpal Spikes stack; bait Rupture — a flat 6s — then step in while it is down."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Infinite Duress is a 110s channel — Rupture's knockup cancels it and Feral Scream denies the cast. Leap only once both are spent, never straight into his face."},{"when":"1st item","text":"After Bami's/bruiser item you still out-sustain a low-stack Cho'Gath, but respect a landed W silence that shuts off your Q and R mid-trade."},{"when":"Late","text":"Feast stacks make him tanky, not immune — Jaws of the Beast scales on max health, so it hits harder every stack. Feral Scream is what actually stops the dive."}],"wants":{"you":["Dodge Rupture (Q) then all-in during the cooldown","Chain Q resets and Blood Hunt to sustain through Vorpal Spikes","Ult him before he reaches Feast-relevant health"],"foe":["Land Rupture then W silence to lock your dash and heal","Farm safely and stack Feast to become unkillable","Use knockup + silence to interrupt your Infinite Duress"]},"early":"Level 1-2 you push and poke freely — Cho'Gath has no reliable early trade tool until Rupture and Vorpal Spikes come online, so use Q sustain to bully him off CS. His Q knockup is his only escape, so track its cooldown.","mid":"Level 3 is yours: dodge the telegraphed Rupture and use Jaws of the Beast to win the return trade. From 4 it turns — Feral Scream silences your Q mid-trade on an 11s cooldown, and Rupture cancels Infinite Duress outright, so leap from his flank.","late":"By first item the matchup tips to Cho'Gath — but Feast stacking is not the wall it looks like: Jaws of the Beast deals max-health damage, so every stack feeds your Q. His real answer is Feral Scream, which silences it mid-dive. Take early leads.","whys":["Level 1 is even — Carnivore keeps him topped up off kills, and Blood Hunt does nothing at full health.","Level 2 is skill — his first point in Rupture or Vorpal Spikes lets him contest, so trades hinge on dodging Q.","Level 3 favours you as Q's heal and Blood Hunt let you win extended trades through his Spikes.","Levels 4-5 go to Cho'Gath — Feral Scream silences Jaws of the Beast and Vorpal Spikes chips you.","Level 6 is his: Rupture cancels a 110s Infinite Duress and Feast is true damage.","At first item his stacked health blunts you and Feral Scream cuts trades.","With 2+ items Cho'Gath wins — Feast health and W silence blunt your dive and execute."]},
  {"a":"warwick","b":"darius","win":["Warwick","Skill","Darius","Skill","Warwick","Darius","Darius"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Fight at range of his Decimate (Q) outer edge — dodge the blade, then Blood-Hunt in and Jaws him while Q is down; your Q heal beats his early bleed if you avoid the outer-ring healing zone."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Infinite Duress suppresses for 1.5s, and a suppressed Darius casts nothing — leap once Apprehend is spent, 26s at rank 1, and burst before Decimate's blade heals him back."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Once Darius has a Stridebreaker/Trinity spike his five-stack bleed plus Guillotine reset can execute you through your sustain, so stop dueling him head-on."},{"when":"Late","text":"Full-stack Darius wins any prolonged fight — his passive bleed out-DPSes your heal and a reset Guillotine punishes your dive; make him chase you into your jungle instead."}],"wants":{"you":["Dodge Decimate's (Q) outer blade then all-in on its cooldown","Ult through his Apprehend pull and Guillotine to cancel them","Win short Blood-Hunt trades before five bleed stacks land"],"foe":["Land the outer edge of Decimate to heal and stack bleed","Apprehend (E) you inward and pin you for a full Q combo","Guillotine-execute you and reset the cooldown to snowball"]},"early":"Level 1-2 you control the wave — Darius wants short-trade Q edges but your Q sustain and Blood Hunt let you disengage the bleed. Never stand in the outer blade of Decimate or you feed his heal and stacks.","mid":"Level 3 is his once Apprehend is online, 4-5 even out, and 6 is yours: Infinite Duress suppresses for 1.5s and he casts nothing through it — burst him before Hemorrhage reaches five stacks and his enrage attack damage switches on.","late":"From first item on, Darius takes over — five-stack bleed out-damages your heal and a reset Noxian Guillotine executes you through Duress. Once he's itemized, refuse the extended duel and pull him under tower or into ganks instead of trading blows.","whys":["Level 1 is yours — Darius can't out-trade your Q sustain and Blood Hunt before his kit comes online.","Level 2 is skill, decided by whether you eat the outer blade of Decimate or dodge it.","Level 3 goes to Darius: Apprehend is online and one pull chains a full Decimate combo.","Levels 4-5 are even as his Q edge-heal and your sustain roughly cancel out.","Level 6 is yours — Infinite Duress cancels his pull and Guillotine to win the all-in.","At first item Darius flips it: his bleed and Guillotine reset out-scale your heal.","With 2+ items Darius wins outright — full-stack bleed and reset execute beat your dive."]},
  {"a":"warwick","b":"drmundo","win":["Warwick","Skill","Warwick","Warwick","Warwick","Warwick","Dr. Mundo"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Blood Hunt gives move speed, not slow immunity — dodge the Bonesaw instead, then dash in. Jaws of the Beast scales on his MAXIMUM health, so every point of HP he builds feeds your bite."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"His passive resists the first immobilising effect on him — spend Primal Howl's fear first, then leap, or Infinite Duress is the one that gets absorbed at 6."},{"when":"1st item","text":"With bruiser sustain you still out-trade a low-HP Mundo, but Maximum Dosage is a flat 120s and heals a percent of MISSING health — the lower he is, the more it returns."},{"when":"Late","text":"Fully-itemised Mundo out-regens you — Infected Bonesaw hits on CURRENT health, his resistances stack, and Maximum Dosage overheals; bring Grievous Wounds or bring your team."}],"wants":{"you":["Dodge his Infected Bonesaw (Q) then dash with Blood Hunt","Fear him first so his passive eats Primal Howl","Trade in short windows while his HP regen is still low"],"foe":["Land Bonesaw (Q) cleavers to chip and slow you","Pop Maximum Dosage to overheal and out-last you","Scale into a health pool your bite cannot out-pace"]},"early":"Level 1-2 you win the wave — Mundo throws Infected Bonesaw (Q) to poke but his early sustain is thin, so use Q heal and Blood Hunt to shove and deny him. Sidestep his cleavers so he burns HP casting them.","mid":"Levels 3-6 are firmly yours: Jaws of the Beast scales on his maximum health, so his own build feeds it and armour does nothing about it. At 6, bait his passive out with Primal Howl's fear before you spend a 110s Infinite Duress on him.","late":"By second item Mundo tips ahead — Maximum Dosage heals a percent of missing health every 120s and his regen out-paces your bite in a solo fight. Stop soloing him; buy Grievous Wounds, catch squishies, and let the team collapse.","whys":["Level 1 is yours — Mundo's early sustain can't match your Q heal and Blood Hunt shove.","Level 2 is skill, hinging on whether you dodge his Bonesaw cleavers.","Level 3 favours you: max-health Q bites harder the more health he stacks.","Levels 4-5 stay yours as your percent-HP Q out-trades his pre-item tankiness.","Level 6 is yours — Duress burst lands before Sadism heal makes him durable.","At first item you still out-trade a low-HP, un-ulted Mundo.","With 2+ items Mundo wins — Maximum Dosage overheals faster than you bite."]},
  {"a":"warwick","b":"fiora","win":["Warwick","Skill","Warwick","Warwick","Skill","Fiora","Fiora"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Before Fiora spikes, Blood Hunt lets you stick through her Lunge (Q) kiting and Jaws-heal beats her early Duelist DPS; force short trades where she can't Riposte (W) your key window."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Riposte parries all incoming damage and stuns whoever it blocks an immobilising effect from — so leaping into it hands her the fight. Bait the 24s W out, then commit."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Once Fiora finishes a first item her vital-proc DPS and true damage out-trade your sustain; her Riposte parries your ult stun window, so stop dueling and play for CD gaps."},{"when":"Late","text":"Full-build Fiora shreds you — Grand Challenge's true damage and its area heal out-pace your Q, and one Riposte turns your leap into a stun on yourself."}],"wants":{"you":["Bait her Riposte (W) then land Infinite Duress after it's down","Stick with Blood Hunt to deny her Lunge (Q) kiting","Force short trades before her Duelist vitals ramp"],"foe":["Riposte (W) your Jaws or Infinite Duress to parry and stun","Proc vitals with Lunge (Q) for true damage and movespeed","Pop Grand Challenge (R) to out-heal your sustain in a duel"]},"early":"Level 1-2 you have the edge — Fiora is fragile before her Duelist ramp, so use Q heal and Blood Hunt to shove and punish any Lunge (Q) she throws to farm. Bait or track her Riposte since it's her only defensive tool.","mid":"Levels 3-5 stay yours: Blood Hunt glues you to her once she drops under 50%, and Jaws of the Beast out-trades her early duel damage. At 6 it evens out — Riposte is 24s at rank 1, and if it blocks your suppression she stuns you, so bait it before you leap.","late":"From first item on Fiora takes over — vital true damage and Grand Challenge lifesteal out-DPS and out-heal your sustain, and one well-timed Riposte parries your Jaws or ult and stuns you. Once she's itemized, avoid the extended duel and only commit when her W is confirmed down.","whys":["Level 1 is yours — Fiora is fragile and can't answer your Q sustain and Blood Hunt shove.","Level 2 is skill, decided by Riposte timing and whether you eat her Lunge vitals.","Level 3 favours you as Blood Hunt sticks to her and your heal wins short trades.","Levels 4-5 stay yours — she can't kite you off and your sustain out-trades her.","Level 6 is even: both ultimates are 110s, and Riposte decides who lands first.","At first item Fiora flips it — vital true damage and R heal out-duel your sustain.","With 2+ items Fiora wins — her DPS, healing, and Riposte parry overwhelm your all-in."]},
  {"a":"warwick","b":"galio","win":["Skill","Galio","Galio","Galio","Galio","Galio","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Blood Hunt lets you close before his Winds of War (Q) tornado ramps damage; dodge the double-tornado overlap, dash in, and Jaws-heal through his weak melee trade since his kit is anti-poke, not anti-dive."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Even at 6 your Duress can lock him, but his Shield of Durand (W) magic-resist channel and Justice Punch (E) knockup can interrupt your ult — bait E before you commit so R lands clean."},{"when":"1st item","text":"His W damage-reduction and E taunt-knockup blunt your all-in, and Galio's magic-resist scaling means your trades stop chunking him — the lane starts slipping."},{"when":"Late","text":"Full-build Galio is an anti-diver — Shield of Durand blunts magic worst, E knocks you out of Duress, and Hero's Entrance (140s) gives him map tempo; win before he itemizes."}],"wants":{"you":["Dodge the Winds of War (Q) converge point, then Jaws in","Bait his Justice Punch (E) knockup before you ult","Hold Primal Howl (E) for his Justice Punch commit"],"foe":["Zone you with Winds of War (Q) magic-damage tornadoes","Interrupt Duress with Justice Punch (E) or Shield channel (W)","Stack MR so Shield of Durand blanks Eternal Hunger"]},"early":"Level 1-2 is close but never free — Winds of War (Q) is 11s at rank 1, so step off the point where the two windblasts converge and take the wave instead. Jaws of the Beast costs 80 mana a bite; do not chase him with it.","mid":"Levels 3-6 belong to Galio: Eternal Hunger is magic damage on every auto and Shield of Durand cuts magic at double the rate it cuts physical, so your autos stop paying. Primal Howl (E, 15s) is the trade-flipper — hold it for his Justice Punch, then Jaws in while E is down.","late":"From first item Galio tips ahead, and Blade of the Ruined King is what pulls you level again — Shield of Durand blunts magic hardest, so %HP physical damage is your way through his resists. His Justice Punch still knocks you out of Infinite Duress, so open with Primal Howl and ult only once that E is spent.","whys":["Level 1 is skill — Eternal Hunger sustains you but Colossal Smash out-ranges every trade.","Level 2 is Galio's — Justice Punch (E) knocks you up before you reach him.","Level 3 is Galio's — Shield of Durand cuts the magic on your autos.","Levels 4-5 stay Galio's — Justice Punch is up every 9s and yours is not.","Level 6 is Galio's — Justice Punch cancels the Infinite Duress channel outright.","At first item Galio's W reduction and MR scaling neutralize your trades.","With 2+ items it evens out — Blade of the Ruined King bites through his resists."]},
  {"a":"warwick","b":"gangplank","win":["Warwick","Skill","Warwick","Warwick","Warwick","Gangplank","Gangplank"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Blood Hunt lets you dive past his Parrrley (Q) poke and Remove Scurvy (W) cleanse doesn't stop your Duress later — force melee range where GP is weakest and Jaws-heal through his Q chip."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Your Infinite Duress locks him through a barrel combo attempt — ult before he detonates a chain, since suppress stops him kiting and denies the Powder Keg zone reset."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Once GP has a Sheen/Trinity spike his barrel-chain burst and Q crit out-trade your dive from range, and Remove Scurvy shrugs your grievous slows — the lane tips to him."},{"when":"Late","text":"Late Gangplank kites your dive entirely — chained Powder Kegs zone and burst you, Q crits shred, and his global R denies your tempo; commit only when his barrels are on cooldown."}],"wants":{"you":["Blood-Hunt past Parrrley (Q) into melee range","Ult him before he can detonate a barrel chain","Fight on top of him where his Keg kiting fails"],"foe":["Poke with Parrrley (Q) and stack barrel chains","Detonate Powder Keg (E) chains to zone and burst you","Cleanse your slow with Remove Scurvy (W) and kite out"]},"early":"Level 1-2 you win — Parrrley is a flat 4.5s at every rank from 625 range, but he has no melee answer, so walk in and Jaws-heal off him. Deny barrel setups by staying on top of him.","mid":"Levels 3-6 are yours: dash past his Q poke with Blood Hunt and Jaws-heal through his chip, keeping the fight in melee where his Kegs can't zone you. At 6, Infinite Duress locks him before he detonates a chain — ult on top of any barrel he places to deny the reset.","late":"From first item Gangplank flips it and by two items he wins outright — Sheen-empowered Q crits and chained Powder Keg (E) detonations burst you from range while Remove Scurvy (W) cleanses your slows. Once he's itemized, only dive when his barrels are down, and use ganks to punish his short trade range.","whys":["Level 1 is yours — GP's poke kit can't stop your Blood Hunt dive and Q shove.","Level 2 is skill, decided by whether you close range or eat Parrrley poke.","Level 3 favours you as you dash into melee and out-sustain his chip.","Levels 4-5 stay yours — he can't zone you with Kegs once you're on top of him.","Level 6 is yours: Duress locks him before he can detonate a barrel chain.","At first item GP flips it — empowered Q crits and barrel burst out-trade your dive.","With 2+ items Gangplank wins — Keg chains, crits, and Scurvy cleanse kite you out."]},
  {"a":"warwick","b":"garen","win":["Garen","Garen","Garen","Garen","Warwick","Garen","Garen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Blood Hunt lets you stick to him through his Decisive Strike (Q) silence-dash; bait the Q, then dash in and Jaws-heal — his Judgment (E) spin is his damage, so trade when E is on cooldown."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Infinite Duress locks Garen through a Judgment spin, and at 6 your execute-scaling burst beats his pre-item tankiness before Demacian Justice (R) can finish you first."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Once Garen has bruiser resistances his Judgment shreds your dive and Q silence cancels your Q and R — his passive regen also out-sustains you between trades."},{"when":"Late","text":"Late Garen out-resists and out-executes you — Judgment DPS, Q silence lockout, and a Demacian Justice execute punish any all-in; refuse the solo duel and catch him out of position instead."}],"wants":{"you":["Bait Decisive Strike (Q) silence then dash in with Blood Hunt","Trade while his Judgment (E) spin is on cooldown","Burst him at 6 before resistances and R scale"],"foe":["Silence you with Decisive Strike (Q) to lock your Q and ult","Shred you with Judgment (E) while stacking resistances","Execute you with Demacian Justice (R) after a trade"]},"early":"Level 1-2 you win — Garen's Decisive Strike (Q) is short-range and his Judgment isn't up, so Blood Hunt in and Q-heal to shove him under tower. Bait his Q silence before you commit anything.","mid":"Levels 3-6 lean your way: dodge or bait his Q, stick with Blood Hunt, and Jaws-heal through his spin, trading hardest when Judgment (E) is down. At 6 your Infinite Duress locks him through a spin and your percent-HP burst beats his pre-item tankiness before Demacian Justice matters.","late":"From first item Garen tips ahead and by two items he wins — resistances blunt Eternal Hunger's magic damage, his Q silence stops you casting Jaws or Duress, and Demacian Justice is true damage on an 80s cooldown late. Stop dueling and punish his lack of escape when he steps up.","whys":["Level 1 is Garen's — Decisive Strike silences you and Perseverance heals it back.","Level 2 is Garen's — Q silence locks Jaws of the Beast out.","Level 3 is Garen's — Judgment out-damages your autos on a 9s cooldown.","Levels 4-5 stay Garen's — Judgment drops to 7.5s while his Q stays flat 8s.","Level 6 is yours: Duress plus percent-HP burst beats his pre-item tankiness.","At first item Garen flips it — resistances and Q silence shut down your dive.","With 2+ items Garen wins — Judgment shred and Demacian Justice execute your all-in."]},
  {"a":"warwick","b":"gnar","win":["Gnar","Gnar","Skill","Skill","Skill","Skill","Warwick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"With Q charged and Blood Hunt tracking a low Gnar you close instantly; his mini-form autos and Boomerang Throw (Q) chip but can't stop your sustain, so trade whenever his Q is on cooldown and heal it back off the wave."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Infinite Duress is a channel and Mega Wallop or GNAR! cancels it, so read his Rage bar rather than his health bar. Ult mini-Gnar, or wait out the Mega window and all-in the frame he reverts, holding Primal Howl for his stun."},{"when":"1st item","text":"This is where Gnar tilts even: once he hits Rage reliably, Mega Gnar's GNAR! (R) wall-stun plus tanky base stats let him bully back, and his boomerang poke out-ranges your engage windows."},{"when":"Late","text":"Mega Gnar flips you into his team with GNAR! on a 30s cooldown at rank 3, and it cancels your ult — but Jaws of the Beast scales off the health he stacks, so bite the tank and spend Duress on somebody else."}],"wants":{"you":["Catch Gnar in mini-form when Blood Hunt marks him low","Q reset trades off the wave to out-sustain his boomerang poke","All-in the transition frame as Mega-Gnar reverts to mini"],"foe":["Reach Rage bar and transform before you commit","Cancel Infinite Duress with Mega Wallop or GNAR!","Kite mini-form with Boomerang Throw and hop (E) resets"]},"early":"Level 1-2 is yours: Eternal Hunger passive sustain plus a charged Jaws of the Beast wins any short trade, and mini-Gnar has no reliable hard CC to punish you, so contest the wave and heal off minions freely.","mid":"From 3 through 6 it stays close; Blood Hunt only speeds you onto a Gnar already under 50% health, and Hop is 22s at rank 1, so the window it is down is the window you fight in. Do not ult into full Rage — Mega Wallop's stun cancels the channel.","late":"Once he stacks health, Jaws of the Beast scales with it, so extended fights start suiting you — the danger is timing, not stats. GNAR! is 30s at rank 3 and cancels Infinite Duress, so open with Primal Howl, eat the stun, then ult.","whys":["Level 1 is Gnar's — Boomerang Throw pokes from 1100 range and your Q reaches 365.","Level 2 stays Gnar's — Hyper is a 7s speed buff he uses to walk back out of reach.","Level 3 is skill — you out-sustain his poke only if you catch him off the hop.","Levels 4-5 are skill — Hop is 17s at rank 3, so fight in the window it is down.","Level 6 is skill — Duress is a channel, and Mega Wallop or GNAR! cancels it outright.","First item is skill — his Bramble Vest blunts the healing that carries your trades.","With 2+ items you win — Jaws of the Beast scales off the health Mega Gnar stacks."]},
  {"a":"warwick","b":"gragas","win":["Skill","Gragas","Skill","Gragas","Gragas","Gragas","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Gragas leans on Barrel Roll (Q) and his Drunken Rage (W) shield-empowered auto to trade; walk up while his Q is on cooldown and Blood Hunt onto him, since your Q reset and Eternal Hunger heal out-sustain his mana-hungry poke."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Infinite Duress leaps further with bonus Move Speed, and Blood Hunt only grants that toward a target under 50% health — chip him first. Body Slam's stun cancels the channel, so fear it out with Primal Howl, then ult."},{"when":"1st item","text":"This is where he tips it: Happy Hour heals him every time he casts a skill, so poke you cannot follow up is free value for him. Freeze instead, and dive only while Body Slam sits on its 13-second cooldown."},{"when":"Late","text":"Late Gragas is a utility bruiser: Explosive Cask knocks you off carries and Drunken Rage cuts the damage he takes. Jaws of the Beast still scales off the health he stacks, so bite him and let your team clean up."}],"wants":{"you":["Walk up and trade when Barrel Roll (Q) is on cooldown","Blood Hunt dive low Gragas and Q-reset off the wave","Fear his Body Slam (E) with Primal Howl then R lock"],"foe":["Poke with Barrel Roll (Q) and E in-and-out safely","Save Explosive Cask (R) to knock you off the all-in","Scale into a tanky utility frontliner past two items"]},"early":"Levels 1-2 favour you: Eternal Hunger sustain and a charged Jaws of the Beast beat Gragas's early Barrel Roll poke, and his mana pool drains fast if he tries to zone you, so contest the wave and heal back any chip.","mid":"From 3 through 6 Gragas holds the edge; Body Slam is 14s at rank 1 and its stun cancels Infinite Duress, so the ult is never a fight starter here — spend Primal Howl on his charge, then bite while that E is down.","late":"With items it levels out: Explosive Cask is 100s at rank 1 and still knocks you off a target, but Jaws of the Beast scales off the health he stacks, so bite the tank and pick your ult target once his Cask is spent.","whys":["Warwick's level 1 sustain and charged Q beat Gragas's early poke.","Level 2 is even as Gragas's Barrel Roll and empowered W poke come online.","Level 3 is skill — Barrel Roll is 8s at rank 3 and Body Slam 13s; fight the gap.","Levels 4-5 are Gragas's — his Body Slam stun cancels your ult.","Level 6 is Gragas's — Explosive Cask knocks you out of the Duress channel.","At first item your R kill threat still punishes squishy Gragas on Blood Hunt marks.","With 2+ items it evens out — Jaws of the Beast scales off the health he stacks."]},
  {"a":"warwick","b":"graves","win":["Warwick","Graves","Skill","Skill","Warwick","Graves","Warwick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Graves's Quickdraw (E) dash plus his shotgun End of the Line (Q) burst make him spike hard around 2-3; respect his all-in when both are up and only trade when his E is on cooldown, using Blood Hunt speed to close so he can't kite with the dash."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Infinite Duress is your equaliser: 1.5s of suppression ends the kite outright. Smoke Screen does not blind, it cuts sight range and slows on impact — so fight inside it if you must, and ult once Quickdraw (16s) is spent."},{"when":"1st item","text":"This is Graves's window; his first item hits hard and every basic attack he lands lowers Quickdraw's cooldown, so it is rarely down when you want it. Play for jungle collapses instead of dueling him."},{"when":"Late","text":"You reclaim the edge late: Blood Hunt gives Move Speed toward anyone under 50% health and attack speed against them, tripling under 25%, so the longer a fight runs the worse his burst looks against your healing."}],"wants":{"you":["Close with Blood Hunt when Quickdraw (E) is on cooldown","R-suppress through Smoke Screen to deny his kiting","Track and run down low Graves late with reveal speed"],"foe":["Burst with shotgun Q and dash out on Quickdraw (E)","Cut your sight with Smoke Screen (W) mid-trade","Spike on first shotgun item and abuse dash spacing"]},"early":"Level 1 is yours on raw sustain, but by 2 Graves spikes: End of the Line detonates after 1 second or on contact with terrain, so never fight him with a wall at your back. Hold back and farm until Jaws of the Beast is up.","mid":"Levels 3-5 stay a skill fight over spacing: at 6 Infinite Duress swings it your way because 1.5s of suppression ends the kite. Hold Primal Howl (15s) for his Quickdraw, then all-in.","late":"Graves's first shotgun item is a real spike that lets him blind-and-burst you, but with your own items you flip the matchup back: Blood Hunt runs down his low-HP escapes and your R plus lifesteal out-duels him in the extended fight.","whys":["Warwick's level 1 sustain edges out Graves before his shotgun spike online.","Graves's level 2 shotgun Q and Quickdraw dash out-trade a gap-closerless Warwick.","Level 3 is an even spacing fight as both trade cooldowns.","Levels 4-5 stay skill-based over dash timing and poke windows.","Level 6 is yours — Duress suppresses for 1.5s and Smoke Screen only cuts sight.","His first item spikes hardest — Quickdraw's cooldown drops as he autos you.","Late you out-duel him — Blood Hunt speeds you at anyone under 50% health."]},
  {"a":"warwick","b":"gwen","win":["Warwick","Skill","Skill","Warwick","Gwen","Gwen","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Gwen is weak and mana-starved early; her Snip Snip (Q) needs stacks to hurt and Skip 'n Slash (E) is her only escape, so Blood Hunt onto her, bait the E, then Q-reset and heal off the wave to keep her permanently low."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Hallowed Mist only stops enemies standing outside it — walk into the cloud and she is targetable again, so step in rather than waiting the 22s out. All-in the moment Skip 'n Slash is down, and hold Primal Howl for her Q so the fear lands mid-burst."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Nightbringer/Riftmaker Gwen starts to spike: her W cloud makes her untargetable to your autos and R lock, and her Q healing lets her outlast trades, so this is where she claws back into the lane."},{"when":"Late","text":"Full-build Gwen shreds tanks with A Thousand Cuts — magic damage scaled to your health that heals her back — while Snip Snip! adds true damage down the centre. Hallowed Mist is 18s at rank 5, so pick her once she has spent it."}],"wants":{"you":["Blood Hunt dive Gwen while she's mana-starved early","Bait Skip 'n Slash (E) then Q-reset and R lock","Freeze the wave and keep her low before her item spike"],"foe":["Reach her item spike and heal off A Thousand Cuts","Hide in Hallowed Mist (W) to dodge your autos and R","Kite with repeated E dashes into the extended fight"]},"early":"You crush Gwen levels 1-3: she's mana-starved, her Q is weak without stacks, and she has no hard CC, so Blood Hunt on cooldown, trade with charged Jaws of the Beast, and heal every scratch back off minions.","mid":"Through 4-6 the lane stays yours; Primal Howl fears her out of aggression, Infinite Duress can lock her before or as she W-clouds, and her only defensive tool is a single E dash you can pre-bait, so keep diving and deny her farm.","late":"Once Gwen finishes items she flips ahead: Hallowed Mist blocks you only from outside the cloud, and A Thousand Cuts — not her Q — is the health-scaling damage that heals her off you, so Executioner's Calling matters more than resists. Trade lane leads for objectives.","whys":["Warwick's sustain and trade power crush a mana-starved level 1 Gwen.","At level 2 Gwen still lacks stacks and CC to answer your Blood Hunt trades.","Level 3 you dive her freely; her single E is her only escape.","Through 4-5 you keep her low with reset trades and fear.","Level 6 Infinite Duress locks Gwen before her W cloud can save her.","At first item her mist plus A Thousand Cuts healing let her outlast you.","Full-build Gwen out-DPSes, out-heals, and disengages your single-target R."]},
  {"a":"warwick","b":"heimerdinger","win":["Warwick","Skill","Heimerdinger","Heimerdinger","Skill","Heimerdinger","Heimerdinger"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Heimerdinger's H-28G Turrets (Q) create a wall of chip that punishes your walk-up; Blood Hunt in when his turrets are freshly placed and force a trade, but around 4-5 a full turret field plus Hextech Micro-Rockets (W) out-zones you and stalls the lane."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Infinite Duress is a channel, so his stun cancels it outright — CH-2 Electron Storm Grenade is a flat 11s at every rank, and those 11 seconds are your whole window. Make him throw it first, then leap; the leap goes further with Blood Hunt speed."},{"when":"1st item","text":"This is Heimer's spike; a completed AP item plus upgraded R turrets makes his zone lethal and his E stun locks your engage, so unless your jungle is diving with you, farm what you can and roam rather than fight into the turret wall."},{"when":"Late","text":"Late Heimerdinger is pure zone control: RPG turret and grenade stun peel you off every all-in, and his poke out-ranges your engage entirely, so split away from his setups and let your team absorb the turret damage."}],"wants":{"you":["Blood Hunt in on freshly-placed turrets before the field stacks","Ult only once the grenade stun has been spent","All-in the frame his Electron Grenade (E) is on cooldown"],"foe":["Stack H-28G Turrets (Q) into a zoning wall","Land CH-2 Electron Grenade (E) stun to cancel your engage","Spike on first AP item and upgraded R turrets"]},"early":"Level 1-3 is your only clear window: before his turret field builds up you can Blood Hunt in, land a charged Q, and force early trades while his E stun is still leveling, so be aggressive immediately or the lane slips away.","mid":"By level 4 his stacked turrets and rockets out-zone you. Infinite Duress can still pick him off the nest, but it is a channel — the grenade cancels it, so count the flat 11 seconds and leap inside that gap, with Primal Howl held for the turrets.","late":"Items make Heimerdinger a fortress: upgraded R turrets and the grenade stun peel every engage and his poke out-ranges you, so stop forcing the losing duel, group with your jungle for dives, and split-push the sidelane he can't defend.","whys":["Warwick's level 1 sustain beats Heimer before his turret field exists.","Level 2 is even as his first turret and grenade come online.","Level 3 is his — H-28 G turrets cost 20 mana on a 1s cooldown.","By 4-5 a full turret wall plus rockets out-zone your walk-up.","Level 6 Infinite Duress lets you drag him off his nest when E is down.","At first item his AP spike and stun turn the zone lethal against you.","Late, Heimer's turret wall and grenade stun peel every all-in you attempt."]},
  {"a":"warwick","b":"illaoi","win":["Warwick","Skill","Illaoi","Illaoi","Warwick","Illaoi","Illaoi"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Illaoi's whole game is landing Test of Spirit (E) to rip your soul; never stand in a spot where her E can pull, and Blood Hunt in only after she misses E or commits Tentacle Smash (Q), then heal the trade back with Eternal Hunger."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Her mobility is Harsh Lesson on a 4-second cooldown, not her ultimate — what Leap of Faith actually does is spawn a tentacle per champion hit. Open with Primal Howl for its 2.5s of damage reduction, then Duress her once she is out of her own field."},{"when":"1st item","text":"This is her window: tentacles spawn on impassible terrain and heal her every time they hit a champion, so a wall at your back is worth more to her than any item. Fight in the open away from terrain, or do not fight."},{"when":"Late","text":"Late Illaoi in her own tentacle nest with R active is one of the strongest teamfighters in the game; if you all-in through a full tentacle field her AoE plus soul-steal out-damages your single-target R, so only engage when her E and R are down."}],"wants":{"you":["Dodge Test of Spirit (E) then Blood Hunt the whiff punish","Open Primal Howl, then Duress outside her field","Sustain non-soul trades and fight away from tentacles"],"foe":["Land Test of Spirit (E) to steal your soul","Fight inside a stacked tentacle field with R up","Grind extended fights near walls where tentacles spawn"]},"early":"Level 1-3 favours you if you respect the E: her Test of Spirit is a skillshot, so juke it, and when she whiffs or commits Q you Blood Hunt in, trade with charged Jaws of the Beast, and heal the chip straight back.","mid":"Through 4-5 she holds the edge: Test of Spirit reaches 900 and Harsh Lesson is a 4s leap that makes every nearby tentacle swing at you. At 6 it turns — Primal Howl's damage reduction then fear walks you out, and Duress finishes it.","late":"Full-build Illaoi flips ahead: inside a stacked tentacle field with R up her AoE and soul-steal out-damage your single-target kit, so never dive her nest, force fights in the open, and only commit when her E and R are on cooldown.","whys":["Warwick's level 1 sustain wins if you dodge Illaoi's early E.","Level 2 is even as her Q and E poke threaten soul-steal.","Level 3 is Illaoi's — Harsh Lesson is a 4s leap onto you.","Levels 4-5 are hers — Test of Spirit reaches 900, your Q 365.","Level 6 Infinite Duress locks her out of her Leap of Faith dance.","At first item her tentacle field out-damages anything you heal back.","Full-build Illaoi's tentacle-field AoE out-damages your single-target R."]},
  {"a":"warwick","b":"irelia","win":["Warwick","Skill","Irelia","Warwick","Irelia","Warwick","Warwick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Irelia is weak before she's stacked and itemized; deny her Bladesurge (Q) resets by not letting minions drop low near you, and Blood Hunt in when her Q is on cooldown so she can't dash away, healing trades with Eternal Hunger."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Infinite Duress is a channel and Flawless Duet's stun cancels it outright, so never open a fight with the ult — bait the E first, hold Primal Howl for the Bladesurge chain, then leap once that 16-second stun is spent."},{"when":"1st item","text":"You hold this stage: Jaws of the Beast scales off her maximum health, so every bruiser item she buys feeds your bite. Trade when Bladesurge (8s at rank 3) is down and let Eternal Hunger pay it back."},{"when":"Late","text":"She still chains Bladesurge resets off low minions, so never fight her beside a wave. Away from one you hold: Eternal Hunger triples below 25% health and Jaws scales off her maximum health, so the longer an isolated duel runs the worse it gets for her."}],"wants":{"you":["Deny Bladesurge (Q) resets by controlling minion HP","Blood Hunt in when her Q is on cooldown","R-lock her before she stacks passive or lands E"],"foe":["Chain Bladesurge (Q) resets to kite and stack passive","Land Flawless Duet (E) stun into full combo","Spike on first item with stacked Ionian Fervor"]},"early":"Levels 1-3 are yours: Irelia is famously weak early with no stacks, so Eternal Hunger sustain and a charged Jaws of the Beast win short trades, and by denying her Q-reset targets you keep her from snowballing.","mid":"Through 4-5 you hold, but 6 is hers: Flawless Duet's stun cancels Infinite Duress, so the ult is a finisher rather than an opener. Defiant Dance only cuts physical damage — Eternal Hunger is magic and goes straight through it.","late":"Her E stun still peels Infinite Duress, so late fights hinge on making her spend it first. Past that you hold the duel: Jaws of the Beast scales off her maximum health and Eternal Hunger triples below 25%, so isolate her away from the wave and never fight beside low minions.","whys":["Warwick's sustain crushes a stackless, itemless level 1 Irelia.","Level 2 is even as her Q poke and reset threat begin.","Level 3 is Irelia's — Flawless Duet stuns you from 850 range.","Through 4-5 Blood Hunt and fear keep her locked out of resets.","Level 6 is hers — her E stun cancels the Infinite Duress channel.","At first item you hold — Jaws of the Beast scales off her max health.","Late you hold the edge — Eternal Hunger triples once you drop under 25%."]},
  {"a":"warwick","b":"jax","win":["Skill","Jax","Jax","Skill","Jax","Jax","Warwick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"With Q gap-close plus W Blood Hunt speed you can force short trades while Jax has no reliable escape, and your P sustain refills the health you spend eating one Q leap."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Counter Strike is 17s at rank 1 and it dodges basic attacks before it stuns, so the ult is not your way in — bait the E, let the dodge window pass, then Duress him inside the 17 seconds it is gone."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Once Jax completes Sheen/Blackcleaver his Q-E-W combo out-DPSes your P healing in an extended fight, so his all-in wins if you stand in Counter Strike."},{"when":"Late","text":"Jax scales past you: his E dodge negates your on-hit poke and his R armor/MR plus stun turns any extended duel in his favor — only engage with jungle or a caught cooldown."}],"wants":{"you":["Short W-speed trades before he hits 3 items","Ulting only after Counter Strike has been spent","Perma-shove and roam once he out-scales you"],"foe":["Landing E stun then Q-resetting onto you","Baiting your R with a fake engage","Reaching Trinity/Cleaver for the extended all-in"]},"early":"Level 1-2 is yours: your P bite and base stats out-trade Jax before he has Q, so contest the first minions and land an auto-heavy poke.","mid":"Through 3-5 you stay ahead on sustain, but the moment Counter Strike goes up Primal Howl is the answer: 2.5s of damage reduction, then a 1s fear, on a 15s timer. Hold the ult until his E is spent.","late":"After first items Jax flips the matchup — his E dodges your poke, his stun locks you, and R makes him tankier, so you cannot solo him; play for shove-and-roam.","whys":["You out-stat Jax at level 1-2 before he has his Q leap.","Level 2 is a skill check as both of you have only one damage ability.","Level 3 your Q plus W speed lets you win short trades over his sustain.","Levels 4-5 are even as Jax's Counter Strike windows trade with your P heal.","Level 6 is Jax's — his E stun cancels your channel if you ult into it.","With his first item Jax's Q-E DPS overtakes your passive sustain.","Late you hold — Jaws of the Beast scales off the health he stacks."]},
  {"a":"warwick","b":"jayce","win":["Jayce","Jayce","Skill","Warwick","Warwick","Warwick","Warwick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Jayce's ranged Q-E poke in Hammer-to-Cannon form chunks you before you reach him, but if you W-speed in and land Q you win the point-blank trade since his melee form has no escape."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Your R Infinite Duress is a full suppress that ignores his Acceleration Gate speed and Thundering Blow knockback, so a level-6 all-in with jungle usually kills him."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Shock Blast fired through Acceleration Gate gains speed, range and damage — but it pushes you under 50%, which is where Eternal Hunger starts healing."},{"when":"Late","text":"Thundering Blow is 20s at rank 1 and knocks you back — that timer is the whole fight. Jaws of the Beast scales off his maximum health, so the stats he buys feed your bite."}],"wants":{"you":["W-speed engaging when his Shock Blast is on cooldown","Ulting through his knockback for a jungle-assisted kill","Freezing to deny his ranged poke advantage"],"foe":["Poking with the Q gate combo from range","Saving E Thundering Blow to peel your all-in","Snowballing the lane with early cannon-form harass"]},"early":"Level 1-2 belongs to Jayce: Shock Blast reaches 600 against your 365 lunge, and Hextech Capacitor gives him Move Speed on every weapon swap. Farm it out.","mid":"Through the mid-levels it swings on his cannon poke — you dominate when you catch him in Hammer form or W-speed onto him, but level 4-5 tilts to Jayce as his ranged Shock Blast combo out-ranges everything you have until 6.","late":"After first item his poke still keeps you out, but Jaws of the Beast deals max-health damage, so every stat he stacks works for you. Perma-shove and let your jungle punish his short escape.","whys":["Level 1-2 favors you as Jayce must go melee to contest CS.","Level 2 is even before both champs have their kits online.","Level 3 is skill — catch him in Hammer form and the trade is yours.","Levels 4-5 turn — Primal Howl's fear breaks the cannon-form combo.","At 6 your R suppress ignores his knockback and speed for a kill.","At first item you hold — his poke drops you under 50%, where you heal.","Late you hold — Jaws of the Beast scales off the health he stacks."]},
  {"a":"warwick","b":"karma","win":["Warwick","Skill","Warwick","Warwick","Warwick","Warwick","Warwick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Karma's only kiting tool is Q Inner Flame plus her RW root-tether, so once you W-speed inside her and land Q you out-sustain her poke every trade."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Your R leaps onto the first champion it hits and suppresses 1.5s — it can miss, and CC cancels the channel, so fire it after she has spent Focused Resolve, not into it."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Karma is a support-item mage top with no reliable escape; your P healing simply outpaces her single-target poke and you kill her on any cooldown mistake."},{"when":"Late","text":"Even scaled, Karma has no way to break your W-speed engage besides Q slow — flash her root or use E's Primal Howl to reset her tether and she folds."}],"wants":{"you":["W-speed diving her through the poke","Ulting to deny her mantra RW root","Running her down whenever her Q is down"],"foe":["Kiting with Q slow and RW root-tether","Poking your P heal down from max range","Calling jungle since she cannot 1v1 you"]},"early":"Level 1-2 is yours: Karma's Q is a slow skillshot and your P bite plus stats let you walk her down and win the first CS trades outright.","mid":"Through the mid-levels you stay firmly ahead — her only peel is Q slow and the RW root, both dodgeable, and your W movement speed closes the gap before her mantra comes back up.","late":"With items you still win: Karma has no dash and no burst to stop your engage, so as long as you save E to cleanse her root or flash it you run her down; she survives only by permanently giving up CS.","whys":["Level 1-2 favors you as your bite beats her slow Q poke.","Level 2 is a skill check before both kits are fully online.","Level 3 your W-speed engage beats her dashless kiting.","Levels 4-5 read even only if she perfectly kites with Q and root.","At 6 your R leap suppresses 1.5s if it lands — bait her root.","With first item your P sustain outpaces her single-target poke.","Late, she has no escape from your engage once her root is used."]},
  {"a":"warwick","b":"kassadin","win":["Warwick","Warwick","Warwick","Warwick","Skill","Warwick","Kassadin"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Pre-6 Kassadin has no Riftwalk escape and low waveclear, so W-speed onto him, land Q, and your P heal beats his Q shield plus E poke every trade."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Your R Infinite Duress suppresses him through the start of a Riftwalk cast — ult the instant he's in range and he can't blink out, turning level 6 into a kill window before he stacks."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Kassadin wants to survive to items, but with Blood Hunt speed and one component you still catch him before Riftwalk's cooldown resets and burst him down."},{"when":"Late","text":"Once Kassadin stacks R and finishes his core, Riftwalk lets him blink away from your engage and his magic burst deletes you before Duress ends — end the game before this."}],"wants":{"you":["Killing him repeatedly before he reaches 6","Ulting to catch him mid-Riftwalk","Denying his stacks so his late spike never lands"],"foe":["Surviving lane to hit his item spike","Blinking away with Riftwalk after 1-2 items","Scaling into unkiteable magic burst"]},"early":"Level 1-2 is yours hard: Kassadin is a melee-weak, escape-less mage early and your P bite plus stats let you shove and dive him off the wave.","mid":"Through the mid-levels you keep the boot on his neck — no dash pre-6 means your W-speed engage always lands, and even at 6 your R can suppress him through a Riftwalk attempt for a kill.","late":"After he completes his core item Kassadin flips it: stacked Riftwalk blinks out of your engage and his burst out-damages your P sustain, so you must snowball a lead and close before two items.","whys":["Level 1-2 favors you against an escape-less early Kassadin.","Level 2 reads even before both kits come online.","Level 3 your W-speed engage beats his dashless kiting.","Levels 4-5 are even as he trades Q shield and E poke.","At 6 your R suppresses him through Riftwalk for a kill.","With first item you still out-speed his Riftwalk cooldown.","Late, stacked Riftwalk and magic burst let Kassadin escape and delete you."]},
  {"a":"warwick","b":"kayle","win":["Warwick","Warwick","Skill","Skill","Kayle","Kayle","Kayle"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Kayle is a melee, immobile weakling before 6 with no waveclear, so W-speed in, land Q, and permanently zone her off XP and CS while your P sustain shrugs off her E poke."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Her level-6 R Divine Judgment gives a few seconds of invulnerability, but you can R-suppress her BEFORE she casts it, or ult and simply wait out the immunity since she can't move away."},{"when":"1st item","text":"This is Kayle's weakest window relative to you — she has no defensive item spike, so keep diving her every wave to deny the stacks she needs; roughly even only if she's farmed safely."},{"when":"Late","text":"Once Kayle hits her level-11 and item spike she out-ranges everything you have, kites with Radiant Blast's slow (8s at rank 5), and her R saves her from your dive — so end early."}],"wants":{"you":["Perma-diving her weak pre-6 laning","Ulting before she can pop Divine Judgment","Denying stacks so her late spike never arrives"],"foe":["Surviving to her level 11 and item spike","Using R invulnerability to negate your all-in","Kiting with ranged E slow once ascended"]},"early":"Level 1-2 you crush her: Kayle is one of the weakest early laners in the game, and your bite plus base stats let you walk her down and deny farm.","mid":"Through the mid-levels you stay dominant — she has no way to stop your W-speed engage, and at 6 you either suppress her before Divine Judgment or bait it out, though the first-item window reads even since neither of you spikes there.","late":"Late Kayle inverts the matchup completely: ranged auto-attacks, Radiant Blast slow kiting, and R invulnerability mean you cannot touch her, so your entire game plan is to snowball a lead and close before she comes online.","whys":["Level 1-2 favors you against the game's weakest early laner.","Level 2 reads even with both kits barely online.","Level 3 your W-speed engage runs down immobile Kayle.","Levels 4-5 are even as she trades E poke for your heal.","At 6 Divine Judgment invulnerability blanks your all-in.","First item is even as neither champion spikes in that window.","Late, ranged kiting and R invulnerability make Kayle unkillable."]},
  {"a":"warwick","b":"kennen","win":["Skill","Kennen","Kennen","Warwick","Kennen","Skill","Warwick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Kennen's Q Thundering Shuriken poke plus E Lightning Rush mobility let him stack Mark of the Storm and stun you before you can commit — his short-cooldown poke chunks you under your P heal."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Your R Infinite Duress suppresses him and eats his Slicing Maelstrom channel if you ult first, so with jungle help level 6 is your best kill window before he gets Zhonya's."},{"when":"1st item","text":"After Kennen buys mobility or Zhonya's, his three-stack stun plus AoE R burst locks and deletes you, and Lightning Rush kites your Q gap-close."},{"when":"Late","text":"Kennen is a ranged, stun-heavy, self-peeling scaler — his R stun-lock and E dashes keep you off him and his burst beats your sustain, so avoid extended fights."}],"wants":{"you":["A level-6 all-in with jungle before his Zhonya's","W-speed committing when Lightning Rush is down","Freezing to limit his ranged Q poke"],"foe":["Stacking Mark of the Storm for the E stun","Kiting your engage with Lightning Rush","Bursting you with R once he has items"]},"early":"Level 1-2 is a coin flip you can win: at level 1 your bite beats him, but the moment he has Q and E his ranged poke and stun stacking start to out-trade you.","mid":"Through the mid-levels Kennen holds the edge — his Q poke and three-stack E stun let him harass you under your heal threshold and disengage with Lightning Rush before you land Q; your one swing back is a level-6 R all-in that suppresses his channel.","late":"Late, Kennen's ranged burst, R stun-lock, and self-peel keep you permanently out of range, so only dive him with a cleanse or jungle CC and otherwise shove and roam.","whys":["Level 1 favors you but is close as his poke comes online fast.","Level 2 tilts to Kennen as his Q and E stun-stacking begin.","Level 3 Kennen's ranged poke and Lightning Rush out-trade you.","Levels 4-5 are yours once you land Q inside his poke.","At 6 Slicing Maelstrom plus a mark stun beats your leap.","First item is even: his stun-lock against your %HP bite.","Late, two items of %max-health bite kill him once you close."]},
  {"a":"warwick","b":"kled","win":["Warwick","Kled","Kled","Kled","Skill","Kled","Warwick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Kled's Q Bear Trap pull plus Violent Tendencies attack-speed shred out-DPS your P heal in any extended trade, and Skaarl's dash makes him hard to pin — respect his all-in."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"His R Chaaaaaaaaarge!!! gives a massive dash and shield on remount, so even if you R-suppress him he often survives and re-engages; only ult with jungle committed."},{"when":"1st item","text":"With Trinity or Cleaver online Kled's Violent Tendencies plus Bear Trap resets shred through you, and losing Skaarl only makes him kite you as ranged Kled with W poke."},{"when":"Late","text":"Kled scales as a tanky bruiser with a huge R engage, courage shields, and sustained shred that beats your dueling — you lose the extended fight almost every time."}],"wants":{"you":["Level-1 aggression before his Q comes online","Ulting only with jungle to secure the kill","Shoving and roaming since he out-duels you"],"foe":["Landing Q Bear Trap to lock a full trade","Shredding you with Violent Tendencies attack speed","Surviving your ult with the R remount shield"]},"early":"Only level 1 is yours: before Kled has his Q Bear Trap your bite and stats win the first exchange, so trade hard immediately.","mid":"From level 2 onward Kled takes over — his Bear Trap pull, Violent Tendencies attack-speed shred, and Skaarl's mobility out-trade your sustain, and even your level-6 R often fails because his remount shield and dash let him survive and re-engage.","late":"Late Kled is a tanky, high-shred bruiser with a game-swinging R engage; he beats you in every extended duel, so your only path is to shove the wave, deny his roams, and let your team punish his over-commits.","whys":["Level 1 favors you before Kled has his Bear Trap.","Level 2 tilts to Kled as Q and Violent Tendencies come online.","Level 3 Kled's Q pull and attack-speed shred out-trade you.","Levels 4-5 favor Kled as his sustained DPS beats your heal.","At 6 Kled's R shield and dash survive your suppression.","With first item Kled's shred and Q resets overpower you.","Late, tanky Kled with a huge R engage wins every duel."]},
  {"a":"warwick","b":"ksante","win":["Skill","K'Sante","K'Sante","K'Sante","Skill","Skill","Warwick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"With all three abilities you out-sustain K'Sante's Ntofo Strikes poke: Q healing plus Eternal Hunger lets you shrug his trades, and once his second Ntofo stack is spent the shockwave pull is gone — burst him with Blood Hunt speed then."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Infinite Duress leaps onto the first champion it hits for a 1.5s suppress and is 110s at rank 1, so he will bait it behind Path Maker's damage reduction (14s) — spend it after that charge, not into it."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Once K'Sante finishes Black Cleaver into tank items his All Out (R) knocks you out of the wall and shreds you in the isolated 1v1; his percent-health true damage on empowered strikes starts outpacing your sustain."},{"when":"Late","text":"Late K'Sante repositions you with All Out, but in that form Path Maker no longer knocks back or stuns and his defenses drop — that is when your %max-health bite kills him."}],"wants":{"you":["Trade at levels 3-5 before his Q charges reset","Save E Primal Howl to cancel his Ntofo Strikes engage","Force fights before he completes his first tank item"],"foe":["Bait your R then All Out you into the wall","Stack Ntofo Strikes charges to poke your sustain down","Scale to two items where his true damage shreds you"]},"early":"Levels 1-2 you're even-to-ahead: your Eternal Hunger sustain absorbs Ntofo Strikes poke, but K'Sante's early Ntofo pull can catch you if you facecheck the wave, so respect his charge count.","mid":"Levels 3-6 are your window. All three abilities online means Q healing plus Blood Hunt speed lets you win extended trades, and at 6 your Infinite Duress locks down his pre-All-Out kit for a clean kill.","late":"Once K'Sante hits his first tank item and can All Out you're behind: he knocks you off him mid-R, his empowered strikes deal percent-health true damage, and every duel favours him past two items.","whys":["Your Eternal Hunger sustain trades evenly with his early Ntofo poke at level 1.","Level 2 is a coin-flip before either of you has a full kit online.","At level 3 your Q heal and Blood Hunt let you win extended trades against his charges.","Through levels 4-5 you out-sustain his Ntofo Strikes poke and can burst him.","At 6 Infinite Duress is a 1.5s leap-suppress; he baits it with Path Maker.","Once he finishes a tank item his All Out knocks you off and true-damage shreds you.","Past two items, All Out's dropped defenses let your %max-health bite kill him."]},
  {"a":"warwick","b":"lillia","win":["Warwick","Warwick","Warwick","Skill","Warwick","Warwick","Warwick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Lillia is a squishy, melee-range dancer who relies on kiting with Blooming Blows (Q); once you W-empower and sink Jaws of the Beast into her she has no early escape and your sustain crushes her non-existent trading."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Watch Out! Eep! (W) is an area nuke, not a dodge — her spacing is Swirlseed (E), a 700-range rolling slow on a flat 12s. Leap once it is spent and Blood Hunt keeps you glued to her."},{"when":"1st item","text":"With Blood Hunt speed and a first item you simply run Lillia down: she has no hard CC to peel your R and no burst to race your Eternal Hunger sustain, so every all-in is yours."},{"when":"Late","text":"Late-game Lillia wants to poke from max range with Q passive movement speed, but a single R connect deletes her; itemize a little MR and she never survives your engage."}],"wants":{"you":["Use Blood Hunt speed to close her kiting gap","All-in with R the instant she wastes Watch Out!","Keep the wave close so she can't poke and dance away"],"foe":["Kite with Blooming Blows passive movement speed","Land Lilting Lullaby sleep to reset spacing","Roam and farm rather than fight you head-on"]},"early":"Levels 1-2 favour you hard: Lillia is a low-base-damage skirmisher and your Eternal Hunger sustain plus early Q healing means she can't win any bump-into-you trade.","mid":"Levels 3-6 stay yours. Blood Hunt movement speed erases her kiting, and at 6 Infinite Duress leaps onto the first champion it hits — fire it once her Swirlseed slow is spent.","late":"Even into items you dominate: Lillia's only tool is poke-and-run, and one R connect with a completed item plus a sliver of MR ends her before her sleep matters.","whys":["Your Eternal Hunger sustain shrugs off her weak level-1 poke.","At level 2 you out-trade her low-damage kit comfortably.","Level 3 gives you Q heal and the tools to punish her melee range.","Levels 4-5 are skill-based as she tries to kite with movement speed.","At 6 Infinite Duress leaps onto her the moment Swirlseed is spent.","A first item plus Blood Hunt speed lets you run her down at will.","Late game one R connect deletes her before her sleep can zone you."]},
  {"a":"warwick","b":"lucian","win":["Warwick","Lucian","Lucian","Skill","Lucian","Skill","Warwick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Lucian owns this window: his Piercing Light (Q) and Ardent Blaze (W) let him poke you from range while Relentless Pursuit (E) dashes away every time you try to walk up, so your Q healing can't keep pace with his double-tap passive chunks."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Even at 6 Lucian holds the edge — Infinite Duress hits the first champion in its path, so he saves Relentless Pursuit (16s at rank 1) to step sideways out of the line. Bait the dash, then leap."},{"when":"1st item","text":"With a first item Lucian's kited damage spikes hard: his passive double-shot plus Ardent Blaze slow means he shreds you before you close, and his E cooldown is low enough to disengage every all-in."},{"when":"Late","text":"By 2+ items you flip back ahead — Blood Hunt speed plus a completed engage tool lets you finally stick to him, and a landed Infinite Duress removes his dash window and deletes the squishy marksman."}],"wants":{"you":["Bait his Relentless Pursuit before committing R","Use minion cover to dodge Piercing Light poke","Scale to 2 items where you finally out-stat him"],"foe":["Poke with Piercing Light and passive double-shots","Kite back with Ardent Blaze slow and E dashes","Hold Relentless Pursuit to escape your Infinite Duress"]},"early":"Level 1 you're even-to-ahead before Lucian has his dash, but from level 2 onward his ranged double-tap poke and Ardent Blaze slow chip you faster than Eternal Hunger heals.","mid":"Levels 2-6 belong to Lucian. He kites with Relentless Pursuit, pokes with Piercing Light, and even at 6 he can E out of your R range, so play safe and farm rather than force.","late":"Once you reach two items the matchup swings: Blood Hunt speed lets you finally run him down, and a single Infinite Duress on the squishy Lucian is a guaranteed kill.","whys":["At level 1 Lucian has no dash yet, so your sustain trades even-to-ahead.","Level 2 gives Lucian Relentless Pursuit and ranged poke that out-trades you.","At 3 his full kit lets him kite and chunk you beyond your heal.","Through levels 4-5 his Ardent Blaze slow and poke keep you at bay.","At 6 he dashes out of Infinite Duress range and can execute with The Culling.","A first item spikes his kited damage and disengage above your sustain.","By two items Blood Hunt speed and one R connect let you delete the squishy Lucian."]},
  {"a":"warwick","b":"malphite","win":["Skill","Warwick","Skill","Skill","Malphite","Malphite","Malphite"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Before Malphite stacks armor you win the trade war: Seismic Shard (Q) poke is mana-hungry, and your Blood Hunt Jaws of the Beast plus Eternal Hunger out-damages Thunderclap (W) once his 10% max-health Granite Shield is popped."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"This is the swing point — Unstoppable Force charges to a location and knocks up, 130s at rank 1, and that hard CC threatens your Duress channel, so bait the charge before you ever leap."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Once Malphite rushes armor his Granite Shield and Ground Slam (E, flat 7s) blunt you — that slam scales off his armor and cuts your attack speed, which is your whole damage. Play his 130s R, not the duel."},{"when":"Late","text":"Late Malphite is a full tank whose R engages your backline and whose armor makes your on-hit sustain damage negligible — he wins every straight-up fight, so use your speed to peel, not to duel him."}],"wants":{"you":["Trade hard at 3-5 while his shield and armor are low","Bait Unstoppable Force before committing R","Farm safely once he completes armor items"],"foe":["Interrupt your Infinite Duress with Unstoppable Force","Rush armor to blunt your on-hit damage","Use passive shield to absorb your trade poke"]},"early":"Levels 1-2 are close: Malphite's passive shield eats your early poke, but before he has mana or Thunderclap online your Eternal Hunger sustain keeps trades even.","mid":"Levels 3-5 are your window to win — his armor and shield aren't stacked yet, so W-empowered Jaws burst plus sustain out-trades him. At 6 it becomes a skill test around his interrupt ult.","late":"Once Malphite buys armor you fall off: Ground Slam scales off it and cuts your attack speed, gutting your on-hit damage, and Seismic Shard steals the move speed you chase with — he wins outright.","whys":["Malphite's passive shield trades evenly with your early poke at level 1.","Level 2 is a skill coin-flip before his kit and mana come online.","At 3 your W-empowered burst out-trades his low early armor.","Through levels 4-5 you win trades before he stacks shield and armor.","At 6 his knockup charge beats your leap and starts his full combo.","His first armor item blunts your on-hit damage back to an even trade.","Full tank Malphite's armor and R engage beat your sustain outright."]},
  {"a":"warwick","b":"maokai","win":["Warwick","Maokai","Maokai","Skill","Maokai","Warwick","Warwick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Before Maokai stacks health you out-trade him: Sapling Toss (E, 18s at rank 1) is his only real poke, and your Blood Hunt Jaws plus Eternal Hunger beats the Bramble Smash (Q, 7s) knockback trade while Sap Magic is on cooldown."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"His Nature's Grasp (R) is a long-range root wave, but if he burns it to engage you can bait it and answer with Infinite Duress; it becomes a skill fight around who lands their CC first."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Once Maokai builds health, Sap Magic — his attack heal, refreshed whenever spells are cast near him — matches your sustain, and Bramble Smash knocks you off while Twisted Advance roots you."},{"when":"Late","text":"Late Maokai is a peel machine — Nature's Grasp roots and Bramble Smash knocks you back off any carry, and his health stacking blunts your on-hit damage, so he wins the extended fight."}],"wants":{"you":["Trade at 3-5 before his health and saplings scale","Bait Bramble Smash knockback before you commit","Force early kills before his tank items come online"],"foe":["Root you with Nature's Grasp to set up a gank","Knock you away with Bramble Smash mid-trade","Out-sustain you with passive sapling heals once tanky"]},"early":"Levels 1-2 are close: Maokai's passive sustain and Sapling poke keep him even, but before his mana and kit scale your Eternal Hunger sustain trades on level terms.","mid":"Levels 2-3 belong to him: Twisted Advance (14s at rank 1) roots you into Bramble Smash, and at 6 Nature's Grasp roots from across the lane — your window is levels 4-5, played on those cooldowns.","late":"Once Maokai buys tank health he flips ahead: passive saplings match your sustain, his W and R chain-CC your engage, and full tank he peels and out-lasts you every time.","whys":["Maokai's passive heal trades evenly with your poke at level 1.","Level 2 is a skill coin-flip before his kit and mana come online.","At 3 his Twisted Advance root chains into a full trade.","Through levels 4-5 you win trades before he stacks tank health.","At 6 Nature's Grasp roots you out of the Duress leap entirely.","His first tank item's health and sustain bring the trade back to even.","Full tank Maokai's chain-CC and health outlast your on-hit damage."]},
  {"a":"warwick","b":"mel","win":["Mel","Skill","Warwick","Warwick","Warwick","Warwick","Warwick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Mel is a squishy ranged mage who leans on Radiant Volley (Q) poke and Rebuttal (W), a barrier that negates damage; your Eternal Hunger sustain out-heals her chip, and once Blood Hunt speeds you in she has no dash to escape."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Infinite Duress locks Mel down, but Solar Snare (E) roots on a 9-11s cooldown and a root kills the leap mid-flight — bait it, then suppress her and the squishy mage simply dies."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Blood Hunt speed erases the range gap a first item gives her — she can't kite a low-health Warwick, and her only peel is a single Solar Snare that you can bait before committing R."},{"when":"Late","text":"Late Mel wants to stack magic damage and poke from max range, but her Overwhelm reflect only matters if you feed her damage; one clean R connect deletes her, so just don't waste your engage into her E."}],"wants":{"you":["Use Blood Hunt speed to close her poke range","Bait Solar Snare before you commit Infinite Duress","All-in the instant she's out of position"],"foe":["Poke with Radiant Volley and self-heal the trade","Root you with Solar Snare to kite away","Reflect your burst with Rebuttal if you dump damage"]},"early":"Levels 1-2 are close as Mel pokes with Radiant Volley from range, but your Eternal Hunger sustain heals the chip and she has no way to punish you beyond harass.","mid":"Levels 3-6 are firmly yours — Blood Hunt speed closes her range, your sustain beats her self-heal, and at 6 Infinite Duress catches the dashless mage for a guaranteed kill.","late":"Even into items you stay ahead: Mel is a squishy poke mage whose only peel is Solar Snare, and one R connect ends her before Golden Eclipse detonates Overwhelm.","whys":["Your Eternal Hunger sustain out-heals her level-1 Radiant Volley poke.","Level 2 is a skill fight before you can fully close her range.","At 3 Blood Hunt and sustain let you win once you reach her.","Through levels 4-5 you out-sustain her poke and run her down.","At 6 Infinite Duress catches the dashless mage for a clean kill.","A first item can't out-range Blood Hunt speed, so you stay ahead.","Late game one R connect deletes the squishy mage before Overwhelm matters."]},
  {"a":"warwick","b":"mordekaiser","win":["Skill","Mordekaiser","Warwick","Warwick","Mordekaiser","Warwick","Warwick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"You own the level-3 window before Morde snowballs: Obliterate (Q) is his main damage and it is dodgeable, so Blood Hunt speed plus Eternal Hunger sustain out-trades him while Indestructible (W, 8-12s) is on cooldown."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Realm of Death (R) flips the matchup — a 140s cooldown that drags you into an isolated 1v1 where Darkness Rise and Indestructible snowball, and he steals a chunk of your stats, so bait it before you commit."},{"when":"1st item","text":"With a first item Blade of the Ruined King's max-health hits out-pace Indestructible, but Realm of Death is still a guaranteed pick if he lands the Death's Grasp (E, 16-8s) pull into ult on you."},{"when":"Late","text":"Late Morde is a bruiser-mage who wins every Realm of Death 1v1: Indestructible heals off your damage, Darkness Rise shreds you, and he steals your stats for the duration, so duel him only with his R down."}],"wants":{"you":["Win the level-3 trade before his shield and R come online","Bait Obliterate then W-empower burst him","Hold Primal Howl for his Death's Grasp pull into R"],"foe":["Isolate you with Realm of Death for a stat-stealing 1v1","Pull you in with Death's Grasp (E) into his ult","Out-sustain your on-hit damage with Indestructible shield"]},"early":"Levels 1-2 are close: Morde's Obliterate poke and passive AoE trade with your Eternal Hunger sustain, but before his shield is leveled you can hold even.","mid":"Levels 3-5 are yours — Blood Hunt speed plus Jaws' max-health bite out-trades him while Indestructible is down. At 6 Realm of Death isolates you, so hold Primal Howl and fight once it is spent.","late":"Items suit you: max-health damage beats his health and shield, and Realm of Death is a 100s cooldown — duel him the moment it is spent, avoid him while it is up, and the side lane is yours.","whys":["Obliterate poke and Darkness Rise trade evenly with Eternal Hunger at level 1.","At 2 his Obliterate and Death's Grasp out-trade you pre-Blood Hunt.","At 3 Blood Hunt plus sustain out-trades him while Indestructible is down.","Levels 4-5 stay yours: Jaws' max-health bite beats his shield stacking.","Realm of Death at 6 isolates you into a stat-stealing 1v1 he wins.","Blade of the Ruined King's max-health hits out-pace his shield.","Away from his 100s ultimate you win the duel on max-health damage."]},
  {"a":"warwick","b":"nasus","win":["Warwick","Skill","Warwick","Skill","Warwick","Skill","Nasus"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"With Jaws of the Beast (8s) and Primal Howl online you win extended trades before Nasus has stacks; Blood Hunt only marks him under 50% health, so it finishes fights, never starts them."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Infinite Duress locks Nasus out of Wither and lets you burst him before he can slow you to a crawl; use it the instant he steps up for a cannon stack."},{"when":"1st item","text":"This is the knife-edge: your bruiser item keeps you even, but every Q stack Nasus lands is permanent, so trades that were free at level 3 start hurting."},{"when":"Late","text":"Once Nasus has hundreds of Siphoning Strike stacks, Spirit Fire cuts your armour and an 11s Wither ends your chase; do not solo him past two items."}],"wants":{"you":["End the lane before Nasus stacks — all-in on his Wither cooldown","Save Primal Howl and Infinite Duress to blank his Wither slow","Roam and set up ganks so he falls behind on farm and stacks"],"foe":["Hit level 6 and stack Q safely under tower with Wither for peel","Reach Spirit Fire plus Sheen and out-sustain your Jaws heal","Drag every fight past two items where his Q and Wither dominate"]},"early":"Levels 1-2 are yours: Nasus has no Wither yet and can only farm, so poke him with Q and deny cannon stacks while Blood Hunt marks him when he's low.","mid":"From level 3 to 6 you press — Jaws' max-health bite and Primal Howl win skirmishes, and at 6 Infinite Duress suppresses him straight through Wither; punish hard, because it only gets worse.","late":"Past the first item his permanent Siphoning Strike stacks tip the scales; Spirit Fire cuts your armour and an 11s Wither cripples your all-in, so avoid extended duels and fight beside your jungler.","whys":["Level 1 favours you because Nasus has no Wither or stacks and simply farms while you control the wave.","Level 2 is even since neither of you has a full combo and Nasus just wants to reach Q stacking safely.","Level 3 is yours: Jaws' max-health bite and Primal Howl win trades before stacks matter.","Levels 4-5 are skill-based as Nasus starts landing Q stacks under tower and trades become a tempo race.","Level 6 swings back to you because Infinite Duress suppresses through Wither and bursts him down.","First item is even — your bruiser spike matches his early Sheen and Spirit Fire while stacks slowly accumulate.","Two-plus items favours Nasus: hundreds of Q stacks, Spirit Fire shred, and Wither make him unkillable in a duel."]},
  {"a":"warwick","b":"nautilus","win":["Nautilus","Nautilus","Skill","Warwick","Warwick","Warwick","Nautilus"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Your Q heal and Blood Hunt speed shred Nautilus in extended trades before he can chain his Dredge Line and Riptide slow into a kill."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Infinite Duress locks him for 1.5s and Titan's Wrath (12s) only absorbs damage, never the suppression; open the instant that shield drops."},{"when":"1st item","text":"With a bruiser item and level advantage you out-duel Nautilus cleanly — his low base damage as a tank can't race your Jaws sustain."},{"when":"Late","text":"Nautilus scales into an unkillable CC brick: Dredge Line hook, Riptide slow, Depth Charge knockup, and titanic HP mean he peels for his team and survives your all-in."}],"wants":{"you":["Win the lane early while his tank damage is low and yours is high","Bait Dredge Line then all-in the cooldown with Q and R","Hold Primal Howl for his Depth Charge knockup, not for chip"],"foe":["Stall to full build where his CC chain locks you for teammates","Land Dredge Line on you to start an unwinnable engage","Scale HP and armor so your on-hit damage barely dents him"]},"early":"Levels 1-2 favour him — Staggering Blow roots on his first hit and Dredge Line drags you into it, so farm safe and wait for your level-3 spike.","mid":"Levels 3 to 6 turn your way: Jaws' max-health bite beats a tank, and at 6 Infinite Duress pins him 1.5s through Titan's Wrath; punish every step-up once Dredge Line is spent.","late":"Once Nautilus has tank items his Dredge Line, Riptide slow, and Depth Charge knockup make him a walking lockdown; his HP outscales your on-hit and he wins any late duel, so end the game before then.","whys":["Level 1 is his: Staggering Blow roots on his first hit and chains into free autos.","Level 2 is his as well: Dredge Line hooks you into a root chain before Blood Hunt exists.","Level 3 is even: Jaws answers Dredge Line, but his 12s Titan's Wrath eats the burst.","Levels 4-5 stay yours since your sustain and burst outpace his low tank damage in every skirmish.","Level 6 is yours: Infinite Duress suppresses 1.5s and Titan's Wrath blocks damage, not the lock.","First item favours you — your bruiser spike beats a tank whose damage hasn't scaled yet.","Two-plus items swings to Nautilus: full tank HP and a four-piece CC chain let him lock you down and win late duels."]},
  {"a":"warwick","b":"neeko","win":["Neeko","Skill","Warwick","Warwick","Neeko","Warwick","Warwick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"You bully Neeko in melee: your Q heal and Blood Hunt speed close her poke range and punish her before she can stack Tangle-Barbs for the root."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Infinite Duress channels through her Pop Blossom windup and locks her before she can burst — R her the moment she jumps for the ult."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Your bruiser sustain shrugs off her Blooming Burst poke, and Shapesplitter's clone (16-12s) buys her nothing once you are inside her 800-range kit."},{"when":"Late","text":"Neeko stays a squishy caster; if you reach her past the frontline your Jaws burst deletes her, though a landed root plus Pop Blossom can still trade you down."}],"wants":{"you":["Force melee range where her poke and root are hardest to land","Suppress her with Infinite Duress before Pop Blossom detonates","Track the real Neeko through disguises with Blood Hunt"],"foe":["Poke you down with Blooming Burst and land a full Tangle-Barbs root","Use clone and disguise to bait your all-in onto the wrong target","Combo root into Pop Blossom to CC and burst before you close"]},"early":"Levels 1-2 are yours — Neeko is a squishy mage who wants to poke, so walk her down with Q, sustain her Blooming Burst, and mark her with Blood Hunt when she's low.","mid":"Levels 3 to 6 stay in your favour: Jaws' max-health bite beats her poke, and at 6 suppression lands before Pop Blossom resolves; only a clean Tangle-Barbs root, which cancels your leap, turns a trade.","late":"Neeko never builds durability, so your on-hit burst keeps deleting her into the late game; the only real threat is eating a full root-into-Pop-Blossom combo, so save Primal Howl to disengage if she lands it.","whys":["Level 1 favours you because you can walk down a squishy poke mage and win melee range.","Level 2 is yours as your early trade pattern beats her weak double-Q poke.","Level 3 favours you: Jaws' lunge and sustain overwhelm her 800-range poke.","Levels 4-5 are even because a landed Tangle-Barbs root plus Blooming Burst can swing a trade her way.","Level 6 is yours if you suppress her before Pop Blossom's wind-up resolves.","First item favours you as your sustain beats her poke and speed nullifies her clone tricks.","Two-plus items stays yours because Neeko builds no durability and your burst reaches and deletes her."]},
  {"a":"warwick","b":"olaf","win":["Skill","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Olaf","Warwick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Early you match his sustain with the Jaws heal, but Reckless Swing (11-7s) is true damage and Berserker Rage hands him more attack speed and lifesteal the lower he drops."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Infinite Duress suppresses Olaf cleanly — but only if he hasn't ulted; the instant Ragnarok is up he's CC-immune and your R does nothing, so bait it first."},{"when":"1st item","text":"With Ragnarok plus a bruiser item Olaf becomes an unstoppable, lifesteal-healing threat who ignores your Primal Howl slow and out-DPSes your all-in."},{"when":"Late","text":"Reckless Swing's true damage and Berserker Rage lifesteal win his duels; buy Grievous Wounds and never fight into an active Ragnarok."}],"wants":{"you":["Win the level 3-5 window before his lifesteal and Swing scale","Force him to burn Ragnarok early, then all-in the cooldown","Kite with Primal Howl and space around his Undertow axe"],"foe":["Reach Reckless Swing and lifesteal to out-heal your Jaws heal","Pop Ragnarok to become CC-immune and negate your Infinite Duress","Land Undertow slow to stick and grind you down with lifesteal"]},"early":"Levels 1-2 are yours as neither of you spikes yet and you can trade evenly, but pick up Blood Hunt value by marking him when his Undertow whiffs and he's low.","mid":"Level 3 is a brief window, but Berserker Rage's missing-health lifesteal and true-damage Reckless Swing take over by 4-5; your one real edge is Ragnarok's 100s cooldown — bait it out, then suppress him and commit everything.","late":"Past the first item Olaf is a nightmare: Ragnarok blanks your suppression and Primal Howl while he attacks, Reckless Swing is true damage, and Berserker Rage heals him harder the lower he drops — all-in only on his ult cooldown.","whys":["Level 1 is even — neither of you spikes and Undertow is his only reach yet.","Level 2 is his: Reckless Swing is true damage your armour cannot answer.","Level 3 is still his: Reckless Swing's true damage on an 11s cooldown beats your Jaws.","Levels 4-5 are his: Berserker Rage's missing-health lifesteal and Reckless Swing win long trades.","Level 6 is his: Ragnarok's disable immunity blanks Infinite Duress while he keeps swinging.","First item favours Olaf: Ragnarok immunity plus lifesteal and Swing out-duel your all-in.","Two-plus items turns to you: max-health damage plus Grievous Wounds cut through his lifesteal."]},
  {"a":"warwick","b":"ornn","win":["Warwick","Skill","Warwick","Warwick","Warwick","Ornn","Ornn"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Jaws of the Beast heals for damage dealt and Ornn is not tanky yet — punish while Bellows Breath Brittle is his only real damage and his pillar sits on 9-7s."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Infinite Duress suppresses 1.5s, but Volcanic Rupture's slow and pillar can deny the leap — bite first, then ult, while his 140s R is down."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Ornn's first tank item and Brittle from Bellows Breath start flipping trades — his shatter combo does real damage now and your on-hit slows down."},{"when":"Late","text":"With full tank items and upgraded gear Ornn's Brittle shatter, Searing Charge knockup, and ultimate CC make him an unkillable frontline you can't solo."}],"wants":{"you":["End the lane before Ornn buys tank items and Brittle scales","Dodge his Searing Charge dash and punish the whiff with Q and R","Force all-ins level 3-5 while his damage and armor are low"],"foe":["Reach tank items and Brittle to shatter you for a burst of damage","Land Searing Charge into pillar for a knockup and Brittle proc","Scale to two items where his CC and HP make him unkillable"]},"early":"Levels 1-2 favour you — Ornn has no tank items yet and weak early damage, so trade with Q, sustain his poke, and mark him with Blood Hunt when he's low.","mid":"Levels 3 to 6 are yours: Jaws' max-health bite beats him before he stacks armour, and at 6 Infinite Duress suppresses him for 1.5s; punish every skirmish while you still out-damage him.","late":"Once Ornn hits his first tank item the matchup flips — Bellows Breath Brittle lets him shatter you for heavy damage, Searing Charge knocks you up, and his ultimate's Brittle-empowered knockup peels you off, so don't duel him past one item.","whys":["Level 1 favours you because Ornn has no tank items and feeble early damage.","Level 2 is even as both build toward a first spike with no full combo online.","Level 3 favours you: Jaws' max-health bite out-trades his 800-range poke.","Levels 4-5 stay yours since your sustain and burst beat his still-low damage.","Level 6 is yours because Infinite Duress bursts him before Brittle and tank stats matter.","First item favours Ornn: tank stats plus Brittle shatter flip trades in his favor.","Two-plus items stays Ornn's — full tank HP, Brittle, and layered CC make him unkillable in a duel."]},
  {"a":"warwick","b":"pantheon","win":["Warwick","Pantheon","Pantheon","Skill","Warwick","Pantheon","Warwick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"This is Pantheon's window: Comet Spear poke and Shield Vault stun chunk you before your Jaws sustain kicks in, and his early damage beats yours in short trades."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Aegis Assault (22s at rank 1) only blocks damage from the front, so wait it out or hit him from behind — then suppress him for 1.5s and the lane flips back."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Pantheon's lead from the early poke phase still lets his burst combo win short trades, so respect his Shield Vault stun before you commit."},{"when":"Late","text":"Warwick scales past Pantheon: your Blood Hunt speed and Jaws sustain out-duel his falling damage, and he can't block your Infinite Duress all-in forever."}],"wants":{"you":["Survive the level 2-3 poke phase and hit your level 6 spike","Wait out Aegis Assault, then all-in with Infinite Duress","Scale to items where your sustain beats his falling burst"],"foe":["Poke you down with Comet Spear before your Jaws heal ramps","Land Shield Vault stun into a full early burst combo","Snowball the level 2-5 lead before Warwick out-scales him"]},"early":"Level 1 is yours, but from level 2 Pantheon's Comet Spear poke and Shield Vault stun take over — his early burst outdamages you, so play safe, sustain with Q, and don't feed his lead.","mid":"The lane is his through level 3-5 until your level 6 spike: Infinite Duress channels through his Aegis Assault block and lets you all-in, so use your ultimate to reclaim tempo whenever his stun is down.","late":"Warwick out-scales Pantheon hard — his early-game damage falls off while your Blood Hunt speed and Jaws sustain grow, so past the first item you win extended duels as long as you dodge his Shield Vault stun.","whys":["Level 1 favours you before Pantheon's poke tools are online.","Level 2 favours Pantheon as Comet Spear and Shield Vault stun let him win the first trade.","Level 3 stays Pantheon's since his burst combo outdamages your sustain early.","Levels 4-5 are even as your Jaws heal starts to offset his poke and the trade evens out.","Level 6 favours you: Infinite Duress suppresses 1.5s and Aegis Assault only guards his front.","First item favours Pantheon whose early lead and burst combo still win short trades.","Two-plus items swings to you: Pantheon's damage falls off while your sustain and speed out-scale him."]},
  {"a":"warwick","b":"poppy","win":["Warwick","Skill","Warwick","Warwick","Warwick","Warwick","Poppy"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Jaws of the Beast heals for damage dealt and wins extended trades before Poppy is tanky; bait Heroic Charge (14-10s) so she cannot pin you to a wall."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Steadfast Presence (20s at rank 1) stops dashes around her, killing both Jaws and your leap — all-in only once she has spent it, then suppress for 1.5s."},{"when":"1st item","text":"With a bruiser item and level lead you out-duel Poppy cleanly since her tank damage hasn't scaled and your Jaws sustain grinds her down."},{"when":"Late","text":"Poppy's full tank build plus Steadfast Presence dash-block and Keeper's Verdict knockback make her a slippery, unkillable peeler who wins the late duel."}],"wants":{"you":["Win the lane early while her tank damage is low and yours is high","Avoid walls so her Heroic Charge can't stun you against terrain","All-in when Steadfast Presence and Keeper's Verdict are on cooldown"],"foe":["Reach tank items where her HP shrugs off your on-hit damage","Pin you to a wall with Heroic Charge for the extended stun","Cancel your Infinite Duress engage with Keeper's Verdict knockback"]},"early":"Levels 1-2 are yours — Poppy has weak early damage and just wants to farm, so trade with Q, sustain her poke, and mark her with Blood Hunt when she drops low.","mid":"Levels 3 to 6 firmly favour you: Jaws' max-health bite beats her before she stacks armour, and at 6 you suppress her for 1.5s; stay off walls for Heroic Charge and watch her W.","late":"Past two tank items Poppy flips it — her HP outscales your on-hit, Steadfast Presence blocks your dashes and grounds you, and Keeper's Verdict can cancel your all-in, so don't solo her once she's fully built.","whys":["Level 1 favours you because Poppy has feeble early damage and only wants to farm.","Level 2 is even as both build toward a spike with no decisive combo yet.","Level 3 favours you: Jaws' max-health bite out-trades her weak early kit.","Levels 4-5 stay yours since your sustain and burst beat her low tank damage.","Level 6 is yours because Infinite Duress bursts her before her tank stats matter.","First item favours you as your bruiser spike beats a tank whose damage hasn't scaled.","Two-plus items swings to Poppy: full tank HP, dash-block, and knockback win the late duel."]},
  {"a":"warwick","b":"quinn","win":["Warwick","Skill","Warwick","Quinn","Warwick","Quinn","Quinn"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"With Q for the leash-heal and E to cancel her Vault, you can force short trades she can't sustain through — walk her down while your passive ticks and Blood Hunt speed keeps you glued to her."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Blinding Assault greys out your autos, never Infinite Duress — but Vault (12-8s) interrupts the leap, so ult only once she has spent her E."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Once she finishes a lethality item and hits her Blinding Assault (Q) into Vault (E) reset combo cleanly, her burst and disengage outrange your gap-close."},{"when":"Late","text":"Quinn roams and one-shots squishies with Heightened Senses; if she's ahead she kites your R with Vault and Skystrike, so group and force her onto your frontline."}],"wants":{"you":["Land R after she burns Vault (E) so she can't dash out","Use Primal Howl's 2.5s damage reduction on her burst","Perma-shove and dive her before she stacks lethality"],"foe":["Poke you flat with Blinding Assault every cooldown","Vault backward the moment you E or dash in","Roam mid/bot with her ult while you're stuck top"]},"early":"Level 1-2 you out-stat her — a marksman with no early sustain — so hug the wave and punish every auto with Jaws. Her trade tool is Blinding Assault (Q, 11s), which greys out your autos but not your ability damage.","mid":"Levels 3-6 stay yours until she buys items: Primal Howl's fear answers her step-up and Jaws keeps you topped, and at 6 the suppression beats her blind. Bait Vault first — it interrupts your leap.","late":"After her first lethality item Quinn's poke and one-combo burst spike hard — she blinds, Vaults away, and kites your R. Keep sidelanes shoved and only engage when her E is down.","whys":["You out-stat a level-1 marksman with your passive heal and dueling base kit.","Even early skirmish — her Blinding Assault trades against your sustain, neither snowballs.","You out-duel her at 3 with Q sustain and E to eat her Vault engage.","Her Blinding Assault plus Vault reset out-poke and disengage your commit through 4-5.","Infinite Duress beats her blind, but Vault interrupts it — ult after her E and 6 is yours.","Her first lethality item turns Blinding Assault into real burst she can kite behind.","Item Quinn out-ranges and out-roams you, blinding and Vaulting away from your all-in."]},
  {"a":"warwick","b":"renekton","win":["Warwick","Renekton","Renekton","Skill","Warwick","Renekton","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"This is Renekton's window: on full fury he opens with Ruthless Predator (W) for a 1.5s stun, heals off Cull the Meek (Q, 7s), and resets with Slice and Dice — he out-trades you before 6."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Infinite Duress is your equaliser, but Ruthless Predator stuns 0.75s — 1.5s on full fury — and any CC cancels the leap, so ult with his fury bar empty and his W spent."},{"when":"1st item","text":"With a completed bruiser item and fury back online his two Slice and Dice casts and the W stun let him pick the trade and disengage yours."},{"when":"Late","text":"Renekton falls off relative to your scaling; even at parity his all-in needs fury and E charges, so bait those and R him when they're spent."}],"wants":{"you":["Ult him when his fury bar is empty and W can't stun-cancel you","Trade at 6+ where Blood Hunt and R flip his fury advantage","Freeze near your tower so his short E dashes can't safely engage"],"foe":["Fury-stack then all-in with W stun into Q heal","Use both Slice and Dice casts to dodge your Q and reset","Kill you 3-5 before you hit your R spike"]},"early":"Level 1 you're fine — pre-fury Renekton has no stun and your passive out-sustains his slap. Don't feed him fury; poke minions, not him.","mid":"Levels 2-5 are his: full-fury Ruthless Predator (W) stuns you for 1.5s out of everything, Cull the Meek (Q, 7s) heals him through your damage, and Slice and Dice resets his engage. Give ground until 6.","late":"At 6 Infinite Duress flips it — channel him when his fury is empty so W can't interrupt. Past first items it's fury-dependent skill: bait his E charges and W, then commit your R.","whys":["Pre-fury level 1 you out-sustain his slap with no stun on the board yet.","At 2 his Ruthless Predator stun and Cull the Meek heal out-trade you.","Full-fury 3-5 is Renekton's peak — W stun, Q heal, E resets dominate.","Even window at 4-5 as your R comes online against his fading fury lead.","Infinite Duress locks him when his fury and W stun are spent — your spike.","With items his fury-fuelled W stun and double-E mobility pick trades again.","Late game is skill and fury management — his all-in versus your R timing even out."]},
  {"a":"warwick","b":"riven","win":["Skill","Riven","Riven","Skill","Riven","Riven","Warwick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Once Riven has all three Broken Wings (Q) charges plus Valor (E) shield and Ki Burst (W) stun, she animation-cancels burst that shreds you and her mobility ignores your gap-close."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"At 6 Valor (10-6s) and Broken Wings can step out of your leap, and Blade of the Exile gives bonus range plus one Wind Slash — ult only once her E is spent."},{"when":"1st item","text":"With a first bruiser/lethality item her three-Q into W stun into R combo simply one-rotations you before Blood Hunt matters."},{"when":"Late","text":"Two items in, max-health damage and sustain out-last her burst — catch her with Valor and the Q charges spent and she dies."}],"wants":{"you":["Bait out Valor (E) and all three Q charges before you engage","Only R her when her E dash is on cooldown","Farm safe and scale — look for jungle collapses, not solo kills"],"foe":["Q-Q-Q into W Ki Burst stun to lock and burst you","Valor-shield your trade damage and dash out of your R","Snowball early leads with her level-3 all-in"]},"early":"Level 1 you edge her with passive sustain before she has her combo online, so contest the first wave. It's the only phase you're favoured — don't overstay it.","mid":"Levels 2 onward belong to Riven: full Broken Wings (Q) charges, Ki Burst (W) stun and Valor (E) shield let her animation-cancel a burst combo that out-trades you, and her mobility dodges your engage. Play for farm and jungle pressure.","late":"With one item her Q-W-R combo one-rotations you, but by two items your sustain and max-health damage flip it — commit whenever Valor is on cooldown.","whys":["Level 1 you out-sustain her before her Q charges and combo come online.","At 2 her Ki Burst stun and Broken Wings burst start out-trading you.","Full-charge level-3 Riven out-bursts and out-mobilities you hard.","Her Valor shield and Q dashes let her dodge your commit through 4-5.","At 6 Valor dodges the leap and Blade of the Exile adds range and damage.","Her first item makes the Q-W-R combo a clean one-rotation kill.","Late your max-health damage and sustain out-grind her burst once she is caught."]},
  {"a":"warwick","b":"rumble","win":["Rumble","Skill","Rumble","Skill","Warwick","Warwick","Warwick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"In the Danger Zone Flamespitter (Q) melts you while Scrap Shield (W) and the Electro Harpoon (E) slow keep you at range — his heat-boosted rotation out-DPSes your level-3 all-in."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"The Equalizer (R) carpets your path in damage and slow, but it is not terrain — Infinite Duress crosses it; leap once it burns out."},{"when":"1st item","text":"With Liandry's/Haestem online his Flamespitter and Harpoon do percent-health burn that beats your sustain no matter how long the fight runs."},{"when":"Late","text":"Overheating locks him out of every spell for its duration — that silence window is your free R engage, and his 80s R cannot answer it."}],"wants":{"you":["Engage only when Rumble is Overheated and silenced","Save E Primal Howl to reduce his Flamespitter and ult damage","Look for jungle ganks — you can't solo this lane"],"foe":["Sit in the Danger Zone and boosted-Flamespitter you down","Slow you with Electro Harpoon and peel with Scrap Shield","Drop The Equalizer across your all-in path"]},"early":"Level 1 is close but heat-dependent — before Rumble builds heat you can walk up, but the moment he hits the Danger Zone his Q burns you. Don't trust the calm.","mid":"Levels 3-6 hinge on Scrap Shield (W, 6s): when it is down, Q-bite in and hold Primal Howl (E) for his Danger-Zone Flamespitter — 2.5s of damage reduction eats the cone. While W is up, farm and give him nothing.","late":"Liandry's-boosted burn plus The Equalizer (R) zoning keep him ahead through items. Engage only when he's Overheated and silenced, and lean on jungle pressure to break the lane.","whys":["Danger-Zone Flamespitter out-burns you even at level 1 once his heat is up.","Even skill window at 2 before his boosted Q rotation fully comes online.","Boosted Flamespitter plus Harpoon slow out-DPS and kite you at 3.","Trade when Scrap Shield (W) is down — its 6s cooldown gates the 4-5 window.","Infinite Duress suppresses him at 6 through any heat window.","Blade of the Ruined King plus your passive out-sustains his burn.","His Overheat window is your free R engage — one suppress ends him."]},
  {"a":"warwick","b":"ryze","win":["Warwick","Warwick","Warwick","Warwick","Warwick","Skill","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Ryze is immobile and squishy — with Q Jaws to close and E Primal Howl to cut his Overload (Q) poke, you walk him down and force flash before he outscales."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Ryze has no dash or blink: land Infinite Duress and he is suppressed 1.5s with only Flash or his 615-range W to answer you."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Even with Rod/Tear online Ryze has zero mobility to your all-in — Blood Hunt speed plus R runs him down the moment his W root is on cooldown."},{"when":"Late","text":"Ryze scales but stays escape-less in lane; keep him shoved and dive him whenever Rune Prison (W) is down and your R is up."}],"wants":{"you":["Walk him down when Rune Prison (W) is on cooldown","R through his root and burst him with no escape available","Perma-shove and threaten all-in so he can never freely poke"],"foe":["Root you with Rune Prison then kite with Overload spam","Poke you with Q Overload from max range","Survive to teamfights where his Realm Warp scales"]},"early":"Levels 1-2 are yours — Ryze has no early kill pressure and no mobility, so you walk up behind minions and threaten every time his Overload (Q) is on cooldown. Punish his short range with your reach.","mid":"Levels 3-6 you dominate: Q Jaws closes the gap, E Primal Howl blunts his Overload poke and reduces his burst, and at 6 Infinite Duress locks down an escape-less mage. Force him to flash or die.","late":"Ryze wants to scale, but in lane he never gets safe — keep the wave shoved into him and all-in whenever Rune Prison (W) is down. Blood Hunt plus R guarantee you catch him.","whys":["You out-range his kill threat at 1 and punish his cooldowns with your reach.","At 2 he still has no mobility and no way to stop you walking him down.","Level 3 Q-and-E let you close and shred an immobile, squishy mage.","Even window at 4-5 as he can trade Overload poke into your engage windows.","Infinite Duress locks an escape-less Ryze the moment you hit 6.","Mana-stacked Ryze fights back with items; you still catch him with R.","Even late you catch him when Rune Prison (W) is down; grouped, he scales."]},
  {"a":"warwick","b":"sejuani","win":["Warwick","Warwick","Warwick","Warwick","Skill","Warwick","Warwick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Sejuani is a tank with weak lane damage — Jaws of the Beast sustain plus Blood Hunt out-DPS her, and Frost Armor (Passive) fades once you keep damage on her, so shove and threaten early."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Glacial Prison (R) is a skillshot stun and it cancels Infinite Duress mid-suppress — bait it out first, then ult, never the reverse."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Once you have a bruiser item your sustained damage beats her tank stats one-v-one; she needs Winter's Wrath stacks before Permafrost can stun."},{"when":"Late","text":"Sejuani becomes a teamfight engage tool, not a duelist — solo you shred her, but respect her R catching you for a jungle collapse."}],"wants":{"you":["Bait Glacial Prison (R) before you commit your all-in","Out-sustain her weak lane damage and shove for plates","Duel her post-item where your DPS beats her tank stats"],"foe":["Land Glacial Prison (R) to stun-lock your combo","Stack Frost with Winter's Wrath, then Permafrost you","Roam and engage for her jungler with her CC"]},"early":"Level 1 is yours — Sejuani has almost no lane damage and your passive out-sustains her Arctic Assault (Q) poke. Push the wave and set up plate pressure.","mid":"Levels 2-5 are a mix: at 3 you shove and out-DPS her tanky-but-toothless kit, but Winter's Wrath (W) stacks Frost and Permafrost (E) stuns off it on a 1.5s cooldown, so 4-5 is a skill check. Never eat a full W into E.","late":"From 6 on you're favoured again — bait her R, then Infinite Duress and your item DPS shred her tank stats one-v-one. She's an engage tool late, so watch for her setting up ganks rather than dueling.","whys":["You out-sustain Sejuani's near-zero level-1 lane damage with your passive.","Even skill window at 2 as her Arctic Assault and armor stacks come online.","At 3 you shove and out-DPS her tanky but low-damage kit.","Winter's Wrath slows and Permafrost stuns off it, so 4-5 is a wash.","Her Glacial Prison stun is a coin-flip skillshot the moment she hits 6.","Post-item your bruiser DPS beats her tank stats in a straight duel.","Late solo you shred her — she's an engage tool, not a duelist."]},
  {"a":"warwick","b":"sett","win":["Sett","Sett","Sett","Sett","Warwick","Sett","Sett"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Sett's Haymaker (W) grit-shield needs to bank damage first — trade in short bursts with Q Jaws so you empty your combo before he punches, and your sustain wins the exchange."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Ult when his grit bar is empty and Facebreaker (E) is on its 16s cooldown — 1.5s of suppression is longer than he can survive with neither answer."},{"when":"1st item","text":"After first items his grit bar refills faster than you can empty it — trade only in the 18s window after Haymaker (W) has been spent."},{"when":"Late","text":"Sett scales into a bruiser monster: full-build Haymaker true damage plus The Show Stopper (R) suplex flip the duel, so kite his cooldowns and fight with your jungler."}],"wants":{"you":["Trade in bursts so his Haymaker (W) grit bar stays empty","R him at 6 before he lands Facebreaker (E) or W","Duel him early where your sustain beats his grit shield"],"foe":["Bank grit then unload a true-damage Haymaker (W)","Facebreaker (E) stun you and R-suplex you out of position","Scale into his late-game bruiser stats and out-tank you"]},"early":"Level 1 you edge him — before Sett has grit banked his slap is weak and your passive out-sustains it. Push and threaten while his Haymaker (W) is empty.","mid":"Levels 3-6 favour you: trade in bursts so his grit bar never fills, use E Primal Howl to blunt his punch, and at 6 Infinite Duress locks him before Facebreaker (E) or Haymaker land. Empty your combo, then back off before he reloads grit.","late":"Sett out-scales you — a full-build true-damage Haymaker (W) and The Show Stopper (R) suplex turn the duel his way after two-plus items. Respect his grit, kite his E, and bring your jungler for the kill.","whys":["Pre-grit level-1 Sett has a weak slap you out-sustain with your passive.","Even skill window at 2 as his Haymaker grit bar begins to matter.","At 3 your burst trades keep his grit empty and your sustain wins.","Banked-grit Haymaker out-damages your burst trades through 4-5.","Infinite Duress locks him before Facebreaker or Haymaker land at 6.","His first-item Haymaker shield outlasts your Blood Hunt window.","Full-build Sett out-tanks you and his true-damage W plus R suplex win."]},
  {"a":"warwick","b":"shen","win":["Warwick","Skill","Warwick","Warwick","Warwick","Skill","Shen"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"With W Blood Hunt active you outrun Shen's slow and Q Jaws of the Beast heal on his own minions to full-clear his poke; punish every wave he uses Twilight Assault (Q) to shove instead of trade."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Shadow Dash (E) taunts you out of Infinite Duress, so ult only once it is down — 18s at rank 1 — and then he cannot block or dash back to tower."},{"when":"1st item","text":"A fed Shen turns Stand United (R) into bot-lane kills, so track that 200s timer — and if he starts the channel inside your 375-range Primal Howl, the fear interrupts it."},{"when":"Late","text":"Late game Shen out-tanks your DPS with Sunfire plus his Q shield and passive, and his global ult swings teamfights — you fall behind unless you snowballed the solo kills."}],"wants":{"you":["Bait Shen to shove so W speed lets you all-in on cooldown","Save R for after his E Shadow Dash is on the floor","Roam or invade with your jungler when his R is down"],"foe":["Use E Shadow Dash to peel your R and taunt you off","Farm safe under tower with Q on minions for the shield","Press R Stand United to save a bot lane and get ahead globally"]},"early":"Level 1 you win the bush and can Q-tick him down, so start strong and deny his Q energy sustain. By level 2 it's Skill — Shen's Q shield off minions blunts your early poke if he plays it right.","mid":"Levels 3-6 are yours: Blood Hunt speed catches him whenever he steps up, and Q healing off his minions keeps you topped through his poke. At 6, bait Shadow Dash (E) first — his taunt cancels your R mid-suppress.","late":"First item you still win the raw 1v1, but Shen's global R and stacking tank items tilt the lane back to Skill and then to Shen — he becomes a peel-and-teamfight problem your solo damage can't answer.","whys":["Level 1 favours you: Warwick wins the bush duel and Q-ticks Shen before he has energy sustain.","Level 2 is skill: Shen's Q shield off minions can neutralize your early poke if timed well.","Level 3 favours you: W Blood Hunt speed catches Shen every time he steps up to CS.","Levels 4-5 favour you: sustained Q healing off his minions keeps you healthy through Shen's poke.","Level 6 favours you: ult once Shadow Dash (E) is spent — his taunt cancels Infinite Duress.","First item is skill: you win the duel but Shen's global R Stand United starts generating map value.","2+ items favour Shen: his tank stats and teamfight ult outscale your single-target DPS."]},
  {"a":"warwick","b":"singed","win":["Warwick","Warwick","Skill","Singed","Singed","Singed","Singed"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Blood Hunt speed lets you stick to Singed as he Fling-and-runs, and Jaws of the Beast healing counters his Poison Trail chip — step up whenever Fling (E) is on its 10s cooldown."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Mega Adhesive (W) grounds you: standing in the goo you cannot Q-lunge or R-leap at all. Ult from clean ground — your leap distance scales with Blood Hunt's move speed."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Once Singed hits Rylai's/Rush of Rod he proxies your wave and out-scales the duel; the lane flips to him because you can no longer catch the slippery poison monster."},{"when":"Late","text":"Late Singed is a permanent chase-me nuisance with Fling flips, huge HP, and Mega Adhesive slows — your R gets baited or Flung and you can't kill him fast enough."}],"wants":{"you":["All-in while your W speed out-paces his Insanity Potion","Use R when Fling (E) and Mega Adhesive (W) are down","Freeze near your tower so he can't proxy safely"],"foe":["Fling (E) you into his tower or his jungler","Drop Mega Adhesive (W) to slow your W chase and root you","Proxy waves and scale with Rylai's to kite you forever"]},"early":"Levels 1-2 are yours: your Q ticks beat his early Poison Trail and he has no Fling until 3 to flip you away. Trade on the wave now — this is the whole window.","mid":"Levels 3-6 are a fight over the goo. Blood Hunt speed closes the gap when Fling (E, 10s) is down, but standing in Mega Adhesive grounds you — no Q lunge, no R leap — so bait the vial out, then commit from clean ground.","late":"After his first big item Singed proxies, scales, and becomes uncatchable — Rylai's and mass HP mean your R gets baited or Flung, so first item and beyond both belong to him.","whys":["Level 1 favours you: Warwick's Q ticks out-trade Singed's early Poison Trail before he has Fling.","Level 2 favours you: with no Fling yet, your Q lunge chunks him on the wave.","Level 3 is skill: Blood Hunt speed sticks to him, but Mega Adhesive grounds your Q.","Levels 4-5 favour Singed: Mega Adhesive grounds your lunge and he kites the trade out.","Level 6 favours Singed: Insanity Potion keeps him over the 50% line Eternal Hunger and Blood Hunt need.","First item favours Singed: Rylai's and proxying let him kite and out-scale the duel.","2+ items favour Singed: mass HP and slows make him uncatchable and your R easily baited."]},
  {"a":"warwick","b":"sion","win":["Skill","Warwick","Warwick","Skill","Skill","Warwick","Warwick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"W Blood Hunt speed lets you weave around his slow, unmissable Q Decimating Smash windup — walk out of the charge, then Q Jaws in for a free trade while it's on cooldown."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"A charged Decimating Smash or Unstoppable Onslaught knocks you out of Infinite Duress mid-channel — ult only after one is spent, and remember killing him wakes an angry zombie."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Sion stacks armor and HP fast, and his passive death-timer means even a won trade doesn't secure the kill — the lane sits at Skill as his tankiness starts to catch your DPS."},{"when":"Late","text":"Late Sion is a wall of HP with a knockup Q, a shield W, and a game-ending Unstoppable Onslaught — but Jaws of the Beast scales off his max health, so his stacking feeds your bite."}],"wants":{"you":["Sidestep his Q charge with W speed, then all-in the cooldown","Save R for after his E and Q are committed","Kill him before his passive revive can trade back"],"foe":["Land a fully-charged Q Decimating Smash to stun and flip the trade","Stack armor/HP and use W shield to blunt your Q burst","Engage or peel with R Unstoppable Onslaught in teamfights"]},"early":"Level 1 you win: your Q ticks beat his slow melee poke and he telegraphs everything. Level 2 is Skill — a landed charged Q stun can swing a trade hard, so respect the windup.","mid":"Levels 3-6 are yours. Blood Hunt speed lets you juke the Q charge and punish its 10s cooldown, Q sustain keeps you healthy, and at 6 you ult only once his charged Q is spent — a knockup cancels it.","late":"By first item Sion's armor and HP stacking pull the lane to Skill, and with two items his tankiness plus his engage/peel ult outscale you — your DPS can't kill him fast and he flips fights.","whys":["Level 1 favours you: Warwick's Q ticks out-trade Sion's slow early poke.","Level 2 is skill: a fully-charged Q Decimating Smash stun can swing the trade his way.","Level 3 favours you: W Blood Hunt speed lets you sidestep the Q charge and punish its cooldown.","Levels 4-5 favour you: Q sustain and speed win every trade where he misses his charge.","Level 6 favours you: R Infinite Duress pins Sion through his knockups for a burst window.","First item is skill: Sion's armor/HP stacking and passive revive start neutralizing your kills.","2+ items favour Sion: mass tankiness plus his engage ult outscale your single-target DPS."]},
  {"a":"warwick","b":"swain","win":["Skill","Skill","Warwick","Swain","Warwick","Swain","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Blood Hunt speed lets you dodge his Vision of Empire (W) zone and close before Nevermove (E) roots you — E is 12s at rank 1, so bait the pull, then commit inside that window."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Ult before Demonic Ascension is running, not after: his R drains every nearby unit, so Grievous Wounds from Executioner's Calling is what makes your 1.5s suppress lethal."},{"when":"1st item","text":"With Rylai's and a Blackfire/health item Swain's E root plus R drain out-sustains your DPS in a straight fight — the lane tilts to him as his AoE heal outpaces your damage."},{"when":"Late","text":"Late Swain is an unkillable AoE drain-tank: land E on you and his R heals through your ult, so you can't solo him and he zones you out of every fight."}],"wants":{"you":["Sidestep his E Nevermove with W speed, then all-in","Ult Swain before his R Demonic Ascension ramps its heal","Kill him early before he stacks HP and drain"],"foe":["Land E Nevermove root to pull you in and start the drain","Ramp R Demonic Ascension so your burst just heals him","Zone the wave with W Vision of Empire and Q poke"]},"early":"Level 1 you win: your Q ticks beat his slow Q barrage before he has E to root you. Level 2 is Skill — his poke and W zone start contesting the wave.","mid":"Level 3 is yours with Blood Hunt speed to dodge E and punish, but Levels 4-5 go to Swain — once he can reliably land E Nevermove the pull-plus-drain flips trades. Level 6 is yours if you ult him before his R ramps; catch him early and burst before the heal snowballs.","late":"After his first item Swain's E-into-R drain out-sustains your damage, and by two items he's an unkillable AoE heal-tank who zones you off every objective — the lane belongs to him.","whys":["Level 1 is even: Eternal Hunger out-sustains chip, but Death's Hand pokes from 750 range.","Level 2 is skill: his Q barrage and W zone start contesting the wave.","Level 3 favours you: W Blood Hunt speed lets you dodge E Nevermove and punish on cooldown.","Levels 4-5 favour Swain: a reliable E root pull plus his drain flips trades in his favor.","Level 6 favours you: R Infinite Duress bursts him if you ult before his R Demonic Ascension ramps.","First item favours Swain: Rylai's and R drain out-sustain your DPS in a straight fight.","2+ items are even: he drain-tanks fights, but Grievous Wounds cuts it back."]},
  {"a":"warwick","b":"sylas","win":["Skill","Warwick","Warwick","Skill","Skill","Warwick","Warwick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Blood Hunt speed lets you dodge Abduct's chain-pull and Chain Lash (Q), then Q-bite in — Kingslayer (W) heals him off you, so trade while his Q sits on its 10s cooldown."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Hijack (R) steals Infinite Duress itself and is 80s at rank 1 — bait the stolen ult out first and only then leap, or you eat your own 1.5s suppression."},{"when":"1st item","text":"You spike harder into a squishy Sylas at first item: your R chunk plus Q sustain out-duels his shield-heal reset if you catch him after Abscond is down."},{"when":"Late","text":"Late you still win the isolated 1v1 — Sylas is squishy and once his mobility is on cooldown your R chains him down before his W heal can save him."}],"wants":{"you":["Dodge his E chain with W speed, then all-in on his cooldowns","Force his stolen R out before you commit Infinite Duress","Isolate him away from his team to secure the 1v1"],"foe":["Poke with Q Chain Lash and heal off you with W","Steal a game-changing ult and dash out with E Abscond","Kite your R window until his mobility comes back up"]},"early":"Level 1 you win: your Q ticks beat his mana-hungry early poke. Level 2 is Skill — his Q Chain Lash and W heal let him trade back if you facecheck.","mid":"Levels 3-4 are yours with Blood Hunt speed to dodge his chain and punish, and Q sustain to shrug his poke. Level 5 is Skill as his combo lands, and at 6 hold Primal Howl (15s) for his all-in — 2.5s of damage reduction, then a fear, breaks it mid-combo.","late":"First item and beyond stay yours: Sylas is squishy, and once you isolate him and his mobility is down your R plus Q melt him before his W shield-heal resets.","whys":["Level 1 favours you: Warwick's Q ticks out-trade Sylas's mana-hungry early poke.","Level 2 is skill: his Q Chain Lash and W heal let him trade back on a facecheck.","Level 3 favours you: W Blood Hunt speed lets you dodge his E chain and punish cooldowns.","Levels 4-5 are mixed but Level 5 is skill: his full combo comes online and can trade evenly.","Level 6 favours you: R Infinite Duress pins him through Abscond before he can escape.","First item favours you: your R chunk plus Q sustain out-duel his squishy shield-heal reset.","2+ items favour you: isolated and low on mobility, Sylas melts to your R before W can save him."]},
  {"a":"warwick","b":"tahmkench","win":["Warwick","Skill","Warwick","Warwick","Warwick","Skill","Tahm Kench"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"W Blood Hunt speed sticks you on Kench, and Q Jaws sustain shrugs his Q Tongue Lash poke — punish him whenever his Q slow is on cooldown before he can stack passive on you."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Abyssal Dive's knockup and a three-stack Tongue Lash stun both cancel Infinite Duress mid-channel — ult only once his W (21s at rank 1) is spent and your stacks are clean."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Kench builds HP and Thick Skin (E) turns stored damage into a shield every 3s; the lane sits at Skill as his self-sustain starts eating your DPS."},{"when":"Late","text":"Late Tahm Kench is a mountain of HP with Thick Skin (E) shielding and a three-stack stun, and Devour (R) pulls an ally straight out of your suppression — bring anti-heal."}],"wants":{"you":["Stick with W speed and trade when his Q Tongue Lash is down","Burst him before three passive stacks proc the stun","All-in early before his HP stacking outpaces you"],"foe":["Land Q Tongue Lash to slow and stack passive toward the stun","Use Abyssal Dive to escape, Devour to save an ally","Stack HP and grey-health to out-sustain your trades"]},"early":"Level 1 you win: your Q ticks out-trade his slow Q poke. Level 2 is Skill — his Q slow and passive stacking start to bite if you overstay in a trade.","mid":"Levels 3-6 are yours. Blood Hunt speed keeps you glued to him and Q sustain beats his Tongue Lash chip — but at 6 hold the ult until Abyssal Dive is spent, because its knockup cancels the channel.","late":"By first item his HP and grey-health regen pull the lane to Skill, and with two items he's a self-peeling HP tank whose devour and passive stun outscale you — your DPS can't break him.","whys":["Level 1 favours you: Warwick's Q ticks out-trade Tahm Kench's slow early poke.","Level 2 is skill: his Q Tongue Lash slow and passive stacking start to punish overstays.","Level 3 favours you: W Blood Hunt speed keeps you glued to Kench for trades.","Levels 4-5 favour you: Q sustain beats his Tongue Lash chip and you win stationary trades.","Level 6 favours you: ult only after Abyssal Dive; its knockup cancels your channel.","First item is skill: his HP stacking and grey-health regen start out-sustaining your trades.","2+ items favour Tahm Kench: mass HP, self-peel devour, and passive stun outscale your DPS."]},
  {"a":"warwick","b":"teemo","win":["Warwick","Skill","Warwick","Teemo","Warwick","Teemo","Teemo"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Blood Hunt speed closes the gap before Teemo can kite, and Jaws of the Beast still lands and still heals while blinded — it is a cast. Commit in the 7s after Blinding Dart."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"R Infinite Duress is un-blindable (it's a channel, not an auto) so you can pin Teemo through his Q Blinding Dart — ult him the instant he steps up to poke."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Once Teemo has Liandry's/Nashor's and shroom control the lane flips: his DoT poke and R Noxious Trap zones out-damage your sustain and blind shuts your resets."},{"when":"Late","text":"Late Teemo is a kiting DoT machine — shroom walls block your W chase, Blinding Dart cancels your auto damage, and his poison out-sustains you from range you can't close."}],"wants":{"you":["All-in with W speed while his Q Blinding Dart is down","Use R Infinite Duress to pin him through the blind","Kill him early before shrooms and Liandry's come online"],"foe":["Blind your autos with Q — your Eternal Hunger heal stops","Kite with Move Quick (W) and poison DoT chip","Wall off with R Noxious Trap shrooms to block your chase"]},"early":"Level 1 you win: your Q ticks out-trade his single auto before he can kite. Level 2 is Skill — his Blinding Dart and poison start to chip and his move speed makes him slippery.","mid":"Level 3 is yours with Blood Hunt speed to catch him, but 4-5 flip to Teemo as blind uptime grows. Hold Primal Howl (15s) for his step-up — 2.5s of damage reduction eats the poke — and at 6 your R is a cast, so blind cannot stop it.","late":"After his first item Teemo's DoT, shroom zoning, and blind out-scale your sustain — first item and beyond both belong to him as he kites you from a range you can't close.","whys":["Level 1 favours you: Warwick's Q ticks out-trade Teemo's single early auto.","Level 2 is skill: his Q Blinding Dart and poison chip start to matter and he's slippery.","Level 3 favours you: W Blood Hunt speed lets you close and all-in before he kites.","Levels 4-5 favour Teemo: growing blind uptime and poke let him win the chip trades.","Level 6 favours you: R Infinite Duress is un-blindable and pins Teemo through his Q.","First item favours Teemo: Liandry's DoT and shroom control out-damage your sustain.","2+ items favour Teemo: kiting poison and shroom walls keep you out of range entirely."]},
  {"a":"warwick","b":"trundle","win":["Trundle","Trundle","Trundle","Trundle","Trundle","Trundle","Skill"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Chomp (Q) saps your attack damage every 3.5s and Frozen Domain (W) amplifies all his healing, so a stand-still trade in his zone feeds him; bite, then step off the domain."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Trundle's Subjugate (R) rips a chunk of your resistances and max health right when you want to all-in with Infinite Duress, so bait his ult or wait it out before you commit."},{"when":"1st item","text":"With a completed bruiser item and Eternal Hunger you finally out-heal his Chomp in long fights; look for a below-50% Trundle to trigger Blood Hunt's speed and lock him with R."},{"when":"Late","text":"Warwick scales into a raid boss with lifesteal and R lockdown while Trundle falls off as a single-target duelist, so drag fights long and hunt low targets across the map."}],"wants":{"you":["Extended fights once your lifesteal and Q healing come online","A sub-50% target to proc Blood Hunt speed and land R","Jungle ganks while his Pillar (E) and R are down"],"foe":["Short bites with Chomp to sap your attack damage","Landing Subjugate before your all-in to swing the stat gap","Pillar (E): terrain that blocks your Q and R dashes"]},"early":"Trundle owns the first levels: Chomp saps your attack damage, slows you, and resets his auto, so a level-1 brawl inside Frozen Domain — where his healing is amplified — goes his way. Farm with Jaws of the Beast, stay out of his 300-range bite, and don't int a trade just because Eternal Hunger is healing you.","mid":"By 3-5 it's even skill: your Q sustain holds, but Subjugate at 6 strips your health and resistances and doubles the theft over 4 seconds. Respect that 120s window, and remember Pillar of Ice is real terrain — it can block your leap.","late":"Once your first bruiser item lands, Eternal Hunger and lifesteal out-sustain his Chomp and you win extended fights; Trundle is a lane bully who fades while Warwick becomes an unkillable hunter that drags low targets down.","whys":["Chomp saps your attack damage, slows, and resets his auto, giving him the level-1 edge.","Level 2 is even as both champs are still farming with single abilities and neither commits.","Level 3 stays skill-based once your Q Jaws sustain answers his early bite trades.","Levels 4-5 remain a coinflip of poke and positioning before either ultimate is online.","Trundle's Subjugate at 6 steals your resistances and max health, tipping the all-in to him.","First item is even as your lifesteal starts closing the gap on his Chomp sustain.","With two-plus items your lifesteal, Q healing, and R lockdown let Warwick out-scale the falling-off Trundle."]},
  {"a":"warwick","b":"tryndamere","win":["Warwick","Warwick","Warwick","Warwick","Skill","Tryndamere","Tryndamere"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Before Tryndamere stacks Fury he has no sustain and low damage, so your Q Jaws heal and Eternal Hunger let you win short trades; punish him whenever his Spinning Slash (E) is on cooldown."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Undying Rage (R) makes him unkillable for 5 seconds, so never blow Infinite Duress on him at full Fury; instead trade him down and save your R to peel or lock him after his ult ends."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Once he has crit and Fury sustain he out-duels you in a straight fight; play for shortened trades and hand him to your jungler rather than a solo all-in."},{"when":"Late","text":"Tryndamere scales into a split-push monster who out-DPSes and out-sustains you 1v1; your value shifts to hunting his carries with R and grouping rather than matching his side lane."}],"wants":{"you":["Short trades before he builds Fury and crit","Punishing his Spinning Slash (E) cooldown windows","Ganks while he lacks the stats to fight back"],"foe":["Stacked Fury and crit items for a sustained duel","Saving Undying Rage (R) to survive your all-in","Splitpushing 1v1 where his DPS and heal snowball"]},"early":"Early Tryndamere is weak: no Fury means no sustain and mediocre auto damage, so your Q Jaws heal and passive out-value his pokes and you take the level-1 and level-3/4 windows. Trade when his Spinning Slash (E) is down and deny his Fury generation off minions.","mid":"Levels 4-5 are even as he starts stacking Fury and crit chance, but the fight flips at 6: Undying Rage guarantees five seconds of survival, so a raw Infinite Duress all-in just wastes your ultimate. Bait or wait out his R before committing lockdown.","late":"With crit items and Fury sustain online Tryndamere out-duels you in a straight fight and becomes a split-push threat, so you stop matching him 1v1. Warwick's late value is hunting his backline with R and Blood Hunt speed while your team pressures elsewhere.","whys":["No Fury means no sustain early, so your Q heal and passive win the level-1 trade.","Level 2 is yours: with no Fury banked his Bloodlust heals nothing.","Level 3 favors you as your Jaws sustain out-values his still-weak, Fury-starved trades.","Levels 4-5 stay yours while he lacks the crit and Fury to punish short trades.","Level 6 is even because Undying Rage negates your all-in but doesn't yet let him kill you.","First item favors Tryndamere as crit and Fury sustain let him out-duel you straight up.","With two-plus items his crit DPS and unkillable ult make him the stronger 1v1 splitpusher."]},
  {"a":"warwick","b":"urgot","win":["Urgot","Urgot","Urgot","Urgot","Urgot","Urgot","Warwick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Urgot's Purge (W) melts you the instant you walk in, and Corrosive Charge (Q) plus his passive shotgun legs zone you off the wave; don't dash in on Q Jaws expecting to trade, you'll lose every exchange."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Fear Beyond Death (R) executes you below the health threshold and drags you in, so keep your bars high and never all-in with Infinite Duress into a healthy Urgot who can just W-Purge and flip you."},{"when":"1st item","text":"With tank items Purge hurts more and by rank 5 it is free — no mana, no cooldown — while Disdain (E) shields him, so farm safe and wait for jungle pressure instead of soloing him."},{"when":"Late","text":"Warwick finally out-scales: with full lifesteal and R lockdown you can flash-R him from fog before he lines up Purge, and team fights let you dodge his slow, clunky shotgun legs."}],"wants":{"you":["Late-game fights where lifesteal and R flanks bypass his poke","Flanking with Blood Hunt speed so he can't line up Purge","Jungle ganks to punish his low early mobility"],"foe":["Standing to W-Purge you the moment you enter melee","Landing Corrosive Charge (Q) and shotgun legs to zone the wave","Executing you with Fear Beyond Death (R) after Purge chunks"]},"early":"This is a losing lane early: Urgot's Purge shreds you the second you step up, Corrosive Charge and his passive legs zone you off farm, and you have no way to trade back through his range. Give up nothing by dashing in on Q Jaws, farm at max range, and accept you'll be down CS.","mid":"It stays rough through 6: Fear Beyond Death executes you below the threshold and yanks you in, so a healthy Urgot beats your Infinite Duress all-in outright when he Purges and flips it. Keep your HP high, ward for his jungler, and lean on your own jungle to make plays.","late":"Warwick's scaling finally pulls ahead with two-plus items: full lifesteal and R lockdown let you flash-R or flank him from fog before he lines up Purge, and messy team fights punish his slow shotgun-leg positioning. Hunt him from angles rather than facechecking his lane.","whys":["Urgot's Purge and shotgun legs out-range and out-damage you from level 1.","Level 2 stays his as Corrosive Charge and Purge zone you off the wave.","Level 3 favors Urgot because you still can't trade through his sustained Purge damage.","Levels 4-5 remain his as his poke and shield keep him healthy while you fall behind.","At 6 Fear Beyond Death executes you and beats your all-in, keeping the edge his.","First item favors Urgot as tank stats and Purge scaling deepen his lane dominance.","With two-plus items Warwick's lifesteal, R lockdown, and flank angles finally out-scale him."]},
  {"a":"warwick","b":"vayne","win":["Vayne","Vayne","Vayne","Vayne","Skill","Vayne","Vayne"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Vayne's Condemn (E) knocks you out of Q Jaws range and can stun you into the wall, while Tumble (Q) resets her spacing every trade; if she lands E you lose the exchange, so bait it before you dash."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Final Hour plus Tumble stealth lets her vanish from your Infinite Duress channel, and Silver Bolts true damage melts your health bar; only all-in when her Condemn is on cooldown and she's cornered."},{"when":"1st item","text":"With attack speed and Silver Bolts online her true-damage DPS out-races your lifesteal, so stop soloing her and collapse with your jungler instead."},{"when":"Late","text":"Vayne is a hyper-carry who shreds tanks and kites you with Condemn and Final Hour stealth; your only path is flanking with R from fog so she can't Tumble or E away before you lock her."}],"wants":{"you":["Baiting out her Condemn (E) before you commit a dash","Flanking from fog so she can't Tumble away from R","Ganks while she has no attack-speed items"],"foe":["Landing Condemn (E) to stun you into a wall","Kiting with Tumble (Q) and Final Hour stealth","Stacking Silver Bolts true damage in extended fights"]},"early":"Vayne wins the early lane: Condemn knocks you out of your Q Jaws range or stuns you into a wall, and Tumble constantly re-spaces so you never get a clean trade. Don't dash in blindly, force her to waste E on a fake commit, and just farm safely while you're the weaker champ.","mid":"Level 5-6 is briefly even skill as your all-in power peaks, but Final Hour and Tumble stealth let her disappear mid-Infinite-Duress, and Silver Bolts true damage chews through your HP. Only commit R when her Condemn is down and she has no room to kite.","late":"Vayne scales into a true-damage hyper-carry who shreds your bruiser build and kites you endlessly with Condemn and stealth. Warwick's only real angle is a fog flank with Blood Hunt speed to lock her before she Tumbles or E's away; otherwise let your team peel and you hunt other targets.","whys":["Vayne's Condemn and Tumble spacing beat your short-range trades from level 1.","Level 2 stays hers as Condemn threatens to stun you out of every commit.","Level 3 favors Vayne because Tumble re-spacing denies your Q Jaws engage.","Levels 4-5 remain hers as her kite tools out-trade your dash-in.","Level 6 is a brief skill window where your peak all-in can catch a mispositioned Vayne.","Her first item lands first: Silver Bolts and Final Hour out-DPS you and escape R.","With two-plus items her true-damage hyper-carry scaling and kiting keep the matchup hers."]},
  {"a":"warwick","b":"vladimir","win":["Warwick","Warwick","Warwick","Warwick","Skill","Vladimir","Vladimir"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Vladimir is weak and mana-less-but-health-costed early, so your Q Jaws heal and Eternal Hunger win short trades; punish him right after he uses Sanguine Pool (W) since it's on a long cooldown and leaves him exposed."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Infinite Duress is a 1.5s suppress on a 110s cooldown, so spend it only once Sanguine Pool is gone — two seconds of untargetability answers the leap if he pools before it connects."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Once Vladimir stacks health and ability haste his Transfusion (Q) sustain and Pool up-time out-heal your damage; stop soloing him and look to the map instead."},{"when":"Late","text":"Vladimir becomes an AoE teamfight monster with Hemoplague (R) amp and constant Pool escapes; your job is to R his backline in fights, not to duel his self-sustaining, untargetable frontline."}],"wants":{"you":["Short trades before he stacks health and haste","Punishing the long Sanguine Pool (W) cooldown","All-in with R while his Pool is unavailable"],"foe":["Scaling health and haste to out-heal you with Transfusion (Q)","Using Sanguine Pool (W) to dodge your R channel","Teamfights where Hemoplague (R) and AoE reign"]},"early":"Vladimir is soft early: his Transfusion costs health and his damage is low, so your Q Jaws heal and passive let you win short trades and deny his farm. The key window is right after Sanguine Pool — it's a long cooldown, so if he burns it to dodge, step up and punish before it's back.","mid":"Levels 4-5 stay yours while his health stacking is thin, and your level-6 all-in is real — but a two-second Pool spent before your leap connects burns the whole 110s ultimate. Commit R only once his W is gone and Blood Hunt is up for the speed.","late":"After his first health/haste item Vladimir's Transfusion sustain and Pool up-time out-heal your DPS, and he snowballs into an AoE teamfight threat with Hemoplague's damage amp. Stop dueling him; use R to lock his carries in fights while your team handles his untouchable frontline.","whys":["Vladimir's health-cost Transfusion and low early damage let your Q heal win level 1.","Level 2 is yours: Transfusion costs him health, and your Q heals what it deals.","Level 3 favors you as your Jaws sustain out-trades his weak early poke.","Levels 4-5 stay yours while he still lacks the health and haste to out-sustain you.","Level 5-6 is even because your all-in is strong but Sanguine Pool can dodge it.","First item favors Vladimir as Transfusion sustain and Pool up-time out-heal your damage.","With two-plus items his AoE teamfight scaling and Hemoplague amp take over the game."]},
  {"a":"warwick","b":"volibear","win":["Warwick","Skill","Volibear","Volibear","Volibear","Volibear","Warwick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Once Volibear has Thundering Smash (Q) stun and Frenzied Maul (W) he out-trades you: his W heals and shreds, his Q stuns if he closes distance, so don't stand still trading and bait his Q by moving unpredictably."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Stormbringer (R) is a 160s leap granting bonus health and disabling your towers — the shield is Sky Splitter (E, 16s), not his ult; never commit Infinite Duress into an up R and his W sustain."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Volibear's bruiser spike with Frenzied Maul heals and Sky Splitter's shield out-sustains your damage in a duel, so farm safely and defer to jungle collapses rather than soloing him."},{"when":"Late","text":"Warwick out-scales into the late game: with full lifesteal and R lockdown you can flank his backline and drag targets down, whereas Voli is a front-to-back diver you can peel and kite in fights."}],"wants":{"you":["Level-1 cheese before his Q stun is online","Late fights where lifesteal and R flanks out-scale him","Baiting his Thundering Smash (Q) so he can't stun-engage"],"foe":["Landing Thundering Smash (Q) stun to lock a trade","Out-sustaining you with Frenzied Maul (W) heals","All-in under Stormbringer (R) shield and tower disable"]},"early":"Level 1 is yours before Volibear has his stun: your Q Jaws and passive win the opening trade if he steps up. But once he hits Thundering Smash and Frenzied Maul at 2-3 the lane flips — his W heals and shreds while his Q stuns any close-range fight, so stop trading toe-to-toe and juke his Q with erratic movement.","mid":"Levels 3 through 6 belong to Volibear: his W sustain out-heals your trades and Stormbringer at 6 is a 160s leap with bonus health and a tower disable that beats your all-in. The shield is Sky Splitter, 16s — don't commit R into an up ultimate; farm safe and wait for your jungler.","late":"The matchup swings back to you with two-plus items: full lifesteal and R lockdown let you flank Voli's team and drag his carries down, while he's a predictable front-line diver you can peel and kite. Play for late team fights, not the mid-game solo duel.","whys":["Level 1 is yours before Volibear's Q stun and W sustain come online.","Level 2 is even as he picks up his kit but can't yet out-trade you cleanly.","Level 3 favors Volibear once Frenzied Maul heal and Thundering Smash stun are online.","Levels 4-5 stay his as his W sustain out-heals your extended trades.","At 6 Stormbringer's bonus health, leap, and tower disable beat your all-in.","First item favors Volibear as his bruiser sustain out-duels you straight up.","With two-plus items Warwick's lifesteal and R flanks out-scale his front-line diving."]},
  {"a":"warwick","b":"wukong","win":["Warwick","Skill","Skill","Skill","Warwick","Wukong","Wukong"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Wukong's Warrior Trickster (W) clone and stealth let him bait your Q Jaws dash and disengage, while Crushing Blow (Q) armor-shred plus Nimbus Strike (E) gap-close even the trades; watch for the decoy before you commit."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Your all-in is strong here, but Cyclone (R) knocks you up and out of Infinite Duress, so only commit R when his ult is down; if you catch him without W or R he's dead to your lockdown."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Wukong's burst spike with armor-pen and Q shred out-trades you in a straight duel, and his W clone escapes your follow-up, so play safe and set up ganks instead of soloing."},{"when":"Late","text":"Wukong scales into a teamfight bruiser whose Cyclone displaces your whole team; your job is to R-lock him or his carry from a flank rather than dueling him where his W and R reset the fight."}],"wants":{"you":["Level-1 and level-6 windows where your all-in beats his cooldowns","Catching him with W clone and Cyclone (R) on cooldown","Ganks while his armor-pen spike isn't online"],"foe":["Baiting your dash with Warrior Trickster (W) clone","Winning trades with Crushing Blow (Q) armor shred","Displacing you out of R with Cyclone (R)"]},"early":"Level 1 is yours: your Q Jaws heal and passive beat Wukong before his kit comes online. Levels 2-4 settle into even skill — his W clone and stealth can bait your dash and his Q shreds your armor, so the trades come down to reading his decoy and not chasing the clone.","mid":"Level 6 swings back to you: your Infinite Duress all-in is strong, and if you catch Wukong with Warrior Trickster and Cyclone on cooldown he simply dies to your lockdown. Just respect that his R knocks you out of the channel, so only commit when his ult is down.","late":"After his first item Wukong's armor-pen burst and Q shred out-trade you in a straight duel, and his W clone escapes your follow-up, so stop soloing him. In team fights his Cyclone displaces your whole line — your value is flanking to R-lock him or his carry rather than dueling where his W and R reset everything.","whys":["Level 1 is yours as your Q heal and passive beat Wukong before his kit is online.","Level 2 is even skill as his W clone and stealth start to answer your trades.","Level 3 stays even with his Q armor shred trading against your Jaws sustain.","Levels 4-5 remain a skill matchup of reading his decoy versus your dash timing.","Level 6 favors you since your all-in kills him when his W and R are down.","First item favors Wukong as armor-pen burst and Q shred out-trade you straight up.","With two-plus items his teamfight Cyclone displacement and W escapes out-scale your solo threat."]},
  {"a":"warwick","b":"yasuo","win":["Warwick","Warwick","Warwick","Warwick","Warwick","Yasuo","Yasuo"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Once Q Jaws of the Beast heals off minions and W Blood Hunt is up, walk him down every time his E Sweeping Blade is on cooldown; he has no reliable way to trade back through your sustain."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Yasuo's R Last Breath comes online and gives him a burst window off any airborne CC, so respect ganks — but 1v1 your R Infinite Duress still beats his kit if you land it clean."},{"when":"1st item","text":"His first crit item (IE or Shieldbow rush) is the point his all-in damage spikes past your Q healing; stop face-tanking and use E Primal Howl's fear to break his tempo."},{"when":"Late","text":"With crit stacked and Wind Wall up on cooldown, Yasuo out-DPSes you in extended fights, so pick him with R engage from fog rather than dueling him even."}],"wants":{"you":["W Blood Hunt active on a low-HP Yasuo to chase him down","fighting while his E Sweeping Blade dashes are on cooldown","short trades where Q sustain refills what his Q tornado poke chips"],"foe":["stacked crit so his auto-attacks out-damage your Q heal","a minion wave to dash through with E for kiting distance","a knock-up from your jungler to combo into R Last Breath"]},"early":"You dominate levels 1-3: Yasuo's early Q Steel Tempest and E Sweeping Blade poke does little against Q Jaws of the Beast healing, and once W Blood Hunt marks him you win any short trade. Don't let him free-farm with E dashes on the wave — step up whenever his dash is down.","mid":"Through levels 4-6 you keep the edge because his Wind Wall only blocks projectiles, not your point-blank R Infinite Duress, and your sustain refills any tornado chip. Look to force all-ins while his E is on cooldown and W is active.","late":"Once Yasuo finishes a crit item the fight flips: his sustained auto DPS plus Wind Wall and R Last Breath off any knock-up outscale your dueling. Play for R engages from fog and let your team follow rather than trading blows straight up.","whys":["Warwick-favoured: Q Jaws healing shrugs off Yasuo's level-1 Steel Tempest poke.","Warwick-favoured: W Blood Hunt lets you punish him the moment his E dash is down.","Warwick-favoured: point-blank R Infinite Duress ignores his Wind Wall so short trades are yours.","Warwick-favoured: your sustain keeps refilling faster than his tornado poke chips you.","Warwick-favoured: at 6 your R still cleanly beats his kit 1v1 before crit comes online.","Yasuo-favoured: his first crit item pushes auto DPS past your Q heal in all-ins.","Yasuo-favoured: stacked crit plus Wind Wall and R Last Breath outscale you in extended fights."]},
  {"a":"warwick","b":"yone","win":["Warwick","Skill","Warwick","Warwick","Warwick","Yone","Yone"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"With Q Jaws of the Beast healing and W Blood Hunt speed, walk Yone down whenever his E Soul Unbound is on cooldown — he can't snap back to safety and your sustain wins the trade."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Yone's R Fate Sealed knocks you toward him for a burst combo, but 1v1 your R Infinite Duress suppresses him out of his Q3 knock-up window if you open with it."},{"when":"1st item","text":"His first crit/on-hit item (Immortal Shieldbow or crit) is when his mixed-damage all-in outpaces your Q heal; stop face-tanking and save E Primal Howl to fear his Q3."},{"when":"Late","text":"With items Yone's E Soul Unbound lets him commit, then snaps his spirit back to his body and repeats part of the damage dealt — pick him with R engage instead."}],"wants":{"you":["W Blood Hunt on a low Yone to run him down before E resets","trading while his E Soul Unbound and Q3 knock-up are on cooldown","short Q-healed trades that beat his early Q Mortal Steel poke"],"foe":["a completed crit or on-hit item so his mixed damage beats your heal","E Soul Unbound up to deal damage then rewind out of your R","landing Q3 knock-up or R Fate Sealed to open a burst combo"]},"early":"Level 1-2 is skill-dependent: Yone's Q Mortal Steel poke and range let him harass, but your Q Jaws of the Beast heal keeps you even if you don't walk into his Q3 knock-up. Farm safely and don't get clipped by his empowered third Q.","mid":"From level 3 on you take over — W Blood Hunt speed lets you close and force trades whenever his E Soul Unbound is down, and your sustain out-values his poke. Punish every E he spends offensively because he can't rewind and disengage at once.","late":"Once Yone completes an item his kit flips the matchup: E Soul Unbound snaps him back to his body and repeats a portion of the damage he dealt, and crit-backed mixed damage overwhelms your Q heal. Play for R Infinite Duress engages from fog and let your team collapse rather than dueling.","whys":["Warwick-favoured: Q Jaws healing holds level 1 despite Yone's Mortal Steel range.","Skill: his Q3 knock-up poke trades even against your sustain if you misposition.","Warwick-favoured: W Blood Hunt lets you punish every offensive E Soul Unbound.","Warwick-favoured: your Q heal out-values his poke while his rewind is down.","Warwick-favoured: at 6 your R suppresses him out of his combo before crit online.","Yone-favoured: his first crit/on-hit item pushes mixed damage past your heal.","Yone-favoured: E Soul Unbound rewind plus crit outscales you in long duels."]},
  {"a":"warwick","b":"yorick","win":["Warwick","Warwick","Skill","Skill","Yorick","Yorick","Yorick"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Before Yorick has a full ghoul pack, all-in him when his E Mourning Mist is on cooldown — without the slow-mark he can't kite you and your Q heal wins the trade."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Yorick's R Eulogy of the Isles spawns Maiden and a wall of ghouls; once his cage is up he can trap you and let ghouls plus autos shred you, so this is where he takes over."},{"when":"1st item","text":"With his first bruiser item and Maiden pushing, Yorick's ghoul DPS out-damages your sustain and his W Dark Procession cage denies your escape; don't dive the wave."},{"when":"Late","text":"Yorick with full ghouls and Maiden out-DPSes and out-splits you; avoid sidelane duels and instead group where his single-target cage matters less."}],"wants":{"you":["all-in windows when his E Mourning Mist slow-mark is on cooldown","fighting before he has a full ghoul pack stacked","short Q-healed trades in the first three levels"],"foe":["a full ghoul pack plus Maiden to stack damage on you","E Mourning Mist landed so ghouls swarm and slow you","W Dark Procession cage to trap you and deny your escape"]},"early":"You own levels 1-2: without a ghoul pack Yorick relies on E Mourning Mist and autos, and your Q Jaws of the Beast heal beats his early trades. Punish him hard before his ghouls come online and W Blood Hunt lets you chase.","mid":"Levels 3-5 turn skill-based as his ghoul pack fills out — he uses E to mark you and swarm with ghouls, so only commit when his E is down. If you let him stack ghouls the trade math flips against your sustain.","late":"From level 6 Yorick takes control: R Eulogy of the Isles adds Maiden and a ghoul wall, and his W Dark Procession cage can trap you for a full ghoul-plus-auto burst. Stop dueling him in the sidelane and group so his single-target kit matters less; his split pressure outscales your dueling.","whys":["Warwick-favoured: Q Jaws healing beats Yorick's level-1 trades before ghouls.","Warwick-favoured: at 2 you still win short trades while his ghoul pack is thin.","Skill: once his ghoul pack builds, trades hinge on dodging his E Mourning Mist.","Skill: E-cooldown windows are even — commit only when his mark is down.","Yorick-favoured: R Eulogy adds Maiden and a ghoul wall that overwhelm your heal.","Yorick-favoured: first item plus Maiden ghoul DPS and W cage beat your sustain.","Yorick-favoured: full ghouls and Maiden out-split and out-DPS you late."]},
  {"a":"warwick","b":"zac","win":["Warwick","Skill","Warwick","Skill","Warwick","Zac","Zac"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Zac heals off his passive blobs, so all-in him after he's spent E Elastic Slingshot or Q Stretching Strikes and before he can pick up blobs — your Q heal plus W Blood Hunt out-sustains him."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Zac's R Let's Bounce brings AoE knock-ups but does little to a 1v1 — your R Infinite Duress still locks him down, so this window stays even-to-yours if you dodge his E engage."},{"when":"1st item","text":"With his first health item Zac's passive blob healing and Q knock-up chains let him tank and reset trades, pulling him back to even against your damage."},{"when":"Late","text":"Fully built, Zac is an unkillable engage tank who bounces in with R and peels — you can't duel him down, so use your R to catch his squishies instead of fighting him."}],"wants":{"you":["all-in after his E Elastic Slingshot and Q are spent and blobs aren't picked up","W Blood Hunt active to out-sustain his passive blob healing","short trades that beat his early poke before he stacks health"],"foe":["a health item so his passive blobs and Q chains reset every trade","picking up passive blobs to heal back the damage you deal","landing E Elastic Slingshot to knock you up and start a chain"]},"early":"Level 1-2 is skill-based: Zac's Q Stretching Strikes has long range and his passive lets him heal off blobs, so short trades can go either way. Keep your Q Jaws of the Beast for the heal and don't eat his E Elastic Slingshot engage.","mid":"Levels 3-5 swing to you — if you all-in right after he uses E and Q, and step on his passive blobs so he can't heal, your Q sustain plus W Blood Hunt speed wins the fight. Deny the blob pickups and he can't reset the trade.","late":"By level 6 Zac's blob healing and Q knock-up chains pull him back to even, and once he has a health item he becomes an unkillable engage tank whose R Let's Bounce peels for his team. Stop trying to duel him and use R Infinite Duress to catch his carries instead.","whys":["Warwick-favoured: Q Jaws healing edges his level-1 trade before blob stacking.","Skill: his long Q range and blob heals make level-2 trades a coin-flip.","Warwick-favoured: all-in after his E/Q spent, denying blobs, wins the fight.","Skill: your Blood Hunt sustain and his blob pickups trade back and forth.","Warwick-favoured: at 6 your R still locks him 1v1 despite his R knock-ups.","Zac-favoured: a health item plus blob healing resets trades faster than you.","Zac-favoured: fully built he's an unkillable engage tank you can't duel down."]},
  {"a":"warwick","b":"ziggs","win":["Warwick","Skill","Warwick","Ziggs","Warwick","Ziggs","Ziggs"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 3-5","text":"Ziggs pokes with Q Bouncing Bomb from max range, but with W Blood Hunt speed and Q Jaws healing you can close the gap when his Q is on cooldown and force a losing trade for him."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Your R is a 110s leap-and-suppress and Satchel Charge is 20s at rank 1 — make him spend the knockback first, then commit; a landed 1.5s lock deletes him, so this window is yours."},{"when":"1st item","text":"Once Ziggs has Luden's or his first AP item, his Q poke and W self-knockback disengage let him zone you off the wave and chip you down before you reach him."},{"when":"Late","text":"With items Ziggs kites you forever — W Satchel bumps you away, E Hexplosive Minefield slows, and his burst outranges your all-in, so flank with R from fog and never facecheck his poke."}],"wants":{"you":["W Blood Hunt speed to close on him while his Q Bouncing Bomb is down","a clean R landed after his W Satchel Charge has been spent","short gap-closes that punish his weak melee-range trading"],"foe":["a completed AP item so Q poke and burst chip you before you reach him","W Satchel Charge up to self-knockback away from your engage","E Hexplosive Minefield placed to slow your approach and kite you"]},"early":"Level 1-2 is skill-based: Ziggs zones with Q Bouncing Bomb and you take chip closing the gap, but Q Jaws of the Beast healing keeps you healthy if you dodge his bombs. Farm what you safely can and wait for your speed spike.","mid":"Level 3 and again at 6 favour you — W Blood Hunt lets you sprint him down when his Q is on cooldown, and R Infinite Duress kills him outright once his W Satchel Charge, 20s at rank 1, has been spent. Land one all-in and he cannot survive it.","late":"Level 4-5 and everything past his first item swing to Ziggs: his AP poke chips you before you arrive, W Satchel bumps you out of range, and E Hexplosive Minefield slows your chase. Don't facecheck his line — flank with R from fog or let your team engage first, because he out-kites and out-ranges your straight-up dive.","whys":["Warwick-favoured: Q Jaws healing shrugs off his level-1 Bouncing Bomb chip.","Skill: closing distance on his Q poke is a trade-off both ways at level 2.","Warwick-favoured: W Blood Hunt speed lets you punish him when his Q is down.","Ziggs-favoured: by 4-5 his Q poke and W disengage zone you off the wave.","Warwick-favoured: at 6 your R kills him if it lands after his Satchel is spent.","Ziggs-favoured: his first AP item chips you down before your dive lands.","Ziggs-favoured: full items let him kite you forever with W, E, and Q range."]}
