window.MC_CONTENT_EXTRA.push({"a":"warwick","b":"masteryi","win":["Warwick","Warwick","Warwick","Skill","Warwick","Skill","Master Yi"],"spikes":[{"when":"Lvl 1-3","text":"Q healing and ramping lifesteal beat his itemless kit in every exchange, and W Blood Hunt runs him down the moment Meditate stops covering the difference."},{"when":"Lvl 6","text":"Meditate is a channel - the 1.5s suppress or a Primal Howl fear ends it outright, and your passive healing finishes the fight the leap starts."},{"when":"1st item","text":"It becomes a skill window: a landed R still kills him, but Alpha Strike goes untargetable (20s at rank 1, cut by his autos) and dodges the leap."},{"when":"Late","text":"His true-damage shred eventually out-races your healing - hand the 1v1 off to your team and spend your suppress as engage instead."}],"wants":{"you":["Early sustain trades he cannot match","R suppress landed before Alpha Strike is up","Kills banked before his true-damage core"],"foe":["Alpha Strike timed to dodge Infinite Duress","Farm into the Wuju true-damage spike","Late duels where shred beats your healing"]},"early":"Levels 1-3 the lane is yours: Q Jaws of the Beast heals through anything he swings back, your ramping lifesteal beats his Meditate math, and W Blood Hunt's speed means any trade that drops him low becomes a chase he cannot escape - bite him on every cooldown and starve his farm.","mid":"Level 4 reads even as you both hunt a window, but level 6 tilts back to you: Meditate is a channel, so the 1.5s suppress ends it, and any commit he makes into your passive-healing frame is a likely death. Into his first item it turns into a skill window - Alpha Strike goes untargetable, so a well-timed one dodges the leap and flips it.","late":"Late game his E Wuju Style true damage finally out-races your healing loop and the sustained duel becomes his - do not chase the 1v1 you owned all laning phase. Convert instead: your suppress is the best engage button on the map, so land it on him or his carries and let your team do the shredding.","whys":["Q healing and ramping lifesteal out-trade him from level 1.","At 2 your sustain beats his Meditate in any exchange.","Level 3 your W run-down and healing keep the trades yours.","Level 4 reads even as you both look for a window.","Your level-6 Infinite Duress suppress makes any commit from him a likely death.","Into his first item it becomes a skill window - your landed R still kills him, but Alpha Strike can dodge the suppress.","Late, his true-damage shred out-heal-races you and wins the duel."]});
